&lt;p&gt;X serves our community of users and customers by working tirelessly to preserve free expression and choice, create limitless interactivity, and create a marketplace that enables the economic success of all its participants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;X is creating a world-class team of media professionals, and is seeking an experienced Client Partner (CP) to develop partnerships and business with Chinese advertisers and their agencies across the world. Experience working with Chinese brands across Gaming, Social and Dating Apps is a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define and drive X’s strategy to grow our partnership with some of the world&#39;s largest largest Chinese brands across the world&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive revenue for X by developing trusted relationships and partnerships with your customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create consultative sales presentations that show how X can help them reach and engage with their customers to grow their business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regularly update your customers on new products, audience insights, and best practice utilization of X&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help your customers create and execute effective campaigns, measure results, and renew partnerships to drive revenue growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that your customers receive the highest level of service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross-functional teams to deliver the best outcomes for customers and for X&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor new team members as our organization grows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in digital media sales, working with Chinese brands and their advertising agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in a fast-paced, dynamic environment and can manage multiple priorities with tight deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative mindset with a proactive approach to problem-solving and cross-functional partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established relationships with marketing decision-makers and their agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of reaching and exceeding sales goals and growing a book of business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build insight-driven sales narratives that support customer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a highly dynamic, rapidly changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aptitude, creativity, and a preference for working in collaborative teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication and presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for X and a genuine appetite to be part of something new&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLIENT PARTNER, GLOBAL BRANDS APAC&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You own brand revenue. This is a hunter role. You will own a portfolio of global brand advertisers across APAC — winning new spend, reactivating lapsed or dormant accounts, and expanding existing partnerships. You are the commercial owner for your book of business: strategy, relationships, pipeline, and revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work as a trusted advisor to brand marketers and their agency partners, building consultative, insight-led programs that put X at the center of both brand and performance plans. You will work as a peer with the Agency Development and X Cross Functional Teams — close partnership, distinct ownership. This role reports to the Head of Global Brands, APAC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and grow revenue across an assigned Global Brands portfolio in APAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hit and exceed quarterly and annual targets through new business, expansion, renewals, and reactivation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hunt and build a disciplined pipeline of net-new and returning advertisers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize client reactivation — bringing lapsed and under-invested global brands back onto the platform with a clear commercial plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and deepen relationships with marketing decision-makers at global brands and with the agencies that plan and buy for them (media, creative, social, and holding-company stakeholders)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deliver consultative sales presentations, QBRs, and joint business plans that connect client objectives to X’s advertising products, audiences, and measurement — in rooms from brand manager to CMO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help advertisers design, launch, and optimize campaigns; measure results; and convert proof into larger, more sustained commitments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with agencies without outsourcing the sale. You own the client outcome even when the buy sits with a holding company or local shop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring market fluency. Know how decisions get made in Singapore, Jakarta, Bangkok, Ho Chi Minh City, Manila and Kuala Lumpur — and adjust the motion accordingly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner tightly with Agency Development, Client Solutions, Marketing, Content Parternships and regional market teams to remove friction and create incremental revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay fluent in the evolving social and digital landscape, X product developments, and competitor activity so you can lead the conversation — not follow it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent X at client meetings, industry events, and in-market reviews across Southeast Asia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in digital advertising sales, advertising technology, or marketing technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working both direct-to-brand and through agency structures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven record of growing a book of business against quota&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed, organized, and effective in a small, high-output team. You do not wait to be told what to sell next&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep working knowledge of both the Southeast Asia advertising markets — how brands plan, how agencies buy, and where decisions actually get made. You have sold in these markets, not just visited them Relationships may be stronger in one market; fluency must cover both&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing, active relationships with global brand clients and their agencies across Southeast Asia. You can open doors in week one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation and storytelling skills. You can hold a room with a CMO, a regional marketing director, and a working-level planner — and leave with a next step&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reactivating dormant, paused, or under-penetrated clients is strongly preferred. You know how to diagnose why spend left and how to win it back&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driven, commercially hungry, and comfortable being measured on revenue. Hunter mentality is non-negotiable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior platform, publisher, social, advertising technology, or marketing technology sales experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency across brand and performance buying&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional Southeast Asia language capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with joint business plans, annual commitments, or multi-market brand coordination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to travel approximately 30% of the time across Southeast Asia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an Industrial Welder to support the buildout of SpaceXSI&#39;s high-performance data centers. In this hands-on role, you will fit and weld large industrial piping and structural steel to ASME Section IX and keep construction moving on our next-generation AI supercomputing infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with mechanical, structural, electrical, and operations teams to weld pipe, supports, and structures from construction through turnover. This is a full-time, onsite role with significant travel to SpaceXSI data center sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fit, tack, and weld large-bore industrial piping and/or structural steel (pipe racks, platforms, supports, skids, and related assemblies) per drawings and ASME Section IX welding procedure specifications (WPS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lay out, cut, bevel, grind, and align joints; check fit-up, root opening, and reinforcement before and after the weld.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read isometric, spool, and structural drawings; work to weld maps, heat numbers, and rod-control / continuity requirements where used.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support hanging of strut, supports, hangers, and structural members; assist with equipment set and bolt-up as needed to complete the weld package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stage, move, and inventory pipe, fittings, structural members, filler metal, and tools; keep laydown yards and work areas orderly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open and close work areas: protection, fire watch and hot-work permits, debris removal, scrap segregation, and end-of-shift reset so the next crew can start immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow LOTO, PPE, hot-work, and site rules; do not weld on live or unpurged systems without authorization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report damaged material, rejected welds, unsafe conditions, and drawing conflicts immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support punch-list, repair, and NDE hold-point work through system turnover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Journey-level industrial construction welding experience: 3+ years welding large industrial piping and/or structural steel, completion of a recognized welding apprenticeship, or equivalent military experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with GTAW (TIG) on stainless steel and/or SMAW (stick) on carbon steel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified to ASME Section IX, or ability to pass a pre-employment weld test to ASME Section IX in the process(es) and position(s) used on site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work at heights, outdoors, and on a changing data center construction site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use welding machines, torches, grinders, and related hand and power tools safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong safety mindset and willingness to follow site procedures, including hot-work permits and LOTO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience on data center, industrial, or heavy-civil construction sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience welding large-bore process, mechanical, or utility piping and heavy structural members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current ASME Section IX qualification (e.g. 6G) in GTAW on stainless and/or SMAW on carbon.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in both TIG-on-stainless and stick-on-carbon; FCAW a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS D1.1 structural welding qualification or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OSHA 10 or equivalent training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read isometric, spool, and structural drawings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel extensively to SpaceXSI data center construction sites and remain onsite during peak construction phases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capability to work in industrial environments, climb ladders, lift and position moderate loads, stand and walk for a full shift, and wear PPE (including welding PPE) for extended periods, with or without reasonable accommodation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMMISSIONING ENGINEER, ELECTRICAL&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an Electrical Commissioning Engineer to execute the buildout, startup, and handover of electrical systems for SpaceXSI&#39;s high-performance data centers. This is a hands-on role where you will commission, test, troubleshoot, and turn over critical systems that support next-generation AI supercomputing infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with construction, engineering, operations, EPC contractors, and OEM vendors to deliver safe, reliable, and high-quality electrical systems. This is a full-time, onsite role with travel to SpaceXSI data center construction sites across the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute all electrical commissioning activities for MV/LV switchgear, generators, UPS systems, PDUs, ATS/STS, transformers, relays, busway, and associated controls in hyperscale data center environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute functional performance testing, pre-functional testing, site acceptance testing, load-bank testing, protection-relay testing, integrated system testing, and system turnover to operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and resolve complex electrical, controls, and process issues during pre-commissioning, commissioning, and startup phases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and review detailed commissioning test procedures, scripts, checklists, and documentation in alignment with project specifications, industry standards, and SpaceXSI requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with EPC contractors, OEM vendors, design engineers, and SpaceXSI stakeholders for system energization, startup sequences, and integrated system validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion safety by enforcing strict adherence to LOTO, NFPA, OSHA, and SpaceXSI safety protocols; participate in daily safety briefings and job hazard analyses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain comprehensive as-built documentation, test records, issue logs, and final commissioning reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and deliver training programs for operations and maintenance teams on commissioned systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in constructability reviews, design feedback sessions, and lessons-learned meetings to continuously improve installation quality and future project execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support commissioning schedules and punch-list resolution to meet aggressive project timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in electrical engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in commissioning for electrical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of commissioning test equipment (power analyzers, insulation testers, hipot testers, torque tools, IR cameras, load banks, relay test sets, etc.), or demonstrated aptitude to learn it in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with relevant codes and standards (NEC, NFPA 70/70B/70E, IEEE, NETA, NESC, Uptime Institute)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read, interpret, and redline electrical drawings, one-lines, three-lines, control schematics, and sequence of operations; update as-built models after commissioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating with multi-discipline teams, contractors, and vendors in construction environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work safely in industrial construction environments and follow LOTO, NFPA, OSHA, and SpaceXSI safety protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commissioning experience, including functional performance testing, pre-functional testing, site acceptance testing, load-bank testing, protection-relay testing, integrated system testing, and system turnover&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data center systems and prior work on mission-critical projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with EPMS, BMS/BAS, and power-system controls troubleshooting and integration (Modbus, BACnet, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of refrigerant systems, direct liquid cooling, and advanced heat rejection technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current OSHA 30 certification or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with commissioning management platforms (CxPro, Procore, PlanGrid, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing integrated systems testing, owner’s project requirements verification, and feeding as-built data back into the sitewide power model (load flow, short-circuit, coordination, arc-flash)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel extensively and work extended hours, nights, and weekends during critical commissioning and startup windows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel extensively to SpaceXSI construction sites and remain onsite for extended periods during peak commissioning phases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physical capability to work in industrial environments, climb ladders/stairs, lift moderate loads (up to 50 lbs), and wear full PPE for long durations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver’s license and ability to meet SpaceXSI&#39;s driver eligibility requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CONSTRUCTION MANAGER, ELECTRICAL&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking an experienced Electrical Construction Manager to lead mission-critical build efforts for our data center in Memphis, Tennessee. As a key on-site leader, you’ll bring credibility, expertise, and steady leadership to fast-paced, high-impact projects. You’ll own site relationships, collaborate with technical and construction teams, and report to central construction leadership, with potential shifts in reporting lines as projects evolve. If you thrive on hands-on leadership, complex industrial electrical construction, and contributing to high-impact AI infrastructure, join us to help deliver one of the most advanced data centers in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the senior construction representative for the Memphis data center, managing relationships with contractors, partners, and internal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee end-to-end project execution, from pre-construction and site development through commissioning and controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate multiple vendors, ensuring seamless communication between field and technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and mitigate risks to ensure high-quality delivery, safety, and operational readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive progress on the data center project, resolving roadblocks to keep timelines on track&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align construction schedules with SpaceXSI&#39;s broader infrastructure goals through cross-functional collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with teams to guide commissioning and resolve issues efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver regular updates using well-designed KPIs and dashboards for internal and external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the project meets technical and quality standards outlined in the base design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform quantity take-offs and field verifications to monitor progress and support reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage change orders, identifying solutions to minimize unnecessary changes and control costs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead site safety initiatives, fostering a consistent and effective safety culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt to evolving needs, supporting cross-functional partners as required, regardless of original job scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience managing data center or construction projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing large-scale data center or mission-critical construction projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in construction management, commissioning, and site operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead on-site with authority and build trust with vendors, partners, and technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing large programs with multiple vendors and dynamic priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills across disciplines, from field updates to technical escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in solving complex, real-time problems with adaptability and composure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in data center construction or highly technical facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with local Memphis building codes and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and ability to handle complex construction challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
