&lt;p&gt;You will oversee electrical contractors and crews building electrical infrastructure for SpaceXSI&#39;s Memphis data center — including underground duct banks, high-voltage and medium-voltage systems, power distribution, grounding, lighting, and process power for mission-critical facilities. If you thrive on hands-on leadership, complex industrial electrical construction, and contributing to high-impact AI infrastructure, join us to help deliver one of the most advanced data centers in the world. If you are a hands-on electrical construction leader who excels in high-stakes, mission-critical environments and is ready to drive the delivery of groundbreaking AI infrastructure, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and coordinate electrical installations including underground duct banks, conduits, cable pulling, terminations, switchgear, transformers, generators, UPS systems, PDUs, and grounding for SpaceXSI data centers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and schedule electrical contractors, subcontractors, and on-site crews to deliver project milestones on time and to SpaceXSI&#39;s exacting quality and reliability standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all contractors adhere to electrical scope, delivering high-integrity power systems critical to data center uptime and operational readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor daily progress of electrical construction, maintaining detailed logs, red-line drawings, and as-built documentation for power infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and enforce aggressive construction schedules while keeping the project on time and within budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion and enforce SpaceXSI&#39;s safety program, building a zero-incident culture across all teams working around energized equipment, excavations, and heavy electrical installations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise foremen and electrical crews, fostering teamwork and accountability in a high-stakes mission-critical environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively resolve on-site challenges — material delays, technical conflicts, sequencing issues, and coordination with other trades — with a strong focus on electrical system reliability and code compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular site inspections to verify compliance with local regulations, electrical codes, safety protocols, and SpaceXSI&#39;s stringent quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and present clear progress reports, electrical construction metrics, and risk updates to senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years managing electrical construction teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of direct hands-on experience in electrical installations including underground duct banks, high-voltage/medium-voltage systems, cable pulling/terminations, switchgear, and power distribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
