&lt;p&gt;Join the High Power Engineering team supporting SpaceXSI to design, build, operate, and maintain electrical infrastructure for AI training campuses. As a Design Engineer on the Data Center team, you will work with a small on-site team to scale high-capacity power systems on a schedule set by compute demand. The position is based in Memphis, TN, with potential travel to other sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce and maintain single-line diagrams, three-lines, panel schedules, cable schedules, conduit and raceway layouts, grounding plans, and equipment elevations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform load calculations, voltage drop, cable ampacity and derating, conduit fill, and pull-tension analysis including long underground runs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Size MV/LV transformers, switchgear, busway, and feeders; specify impedance, BIL, temperature rise, and short-time ratings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write equipment specifications and technical bid evaluations for ring-main units, transformers, switchgear, busway, and PDUs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supply model inputs to protection and power-system studies: nameplate data, impedances, cable constants, and as-designed configurations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve field RFIs and issue design changes during construction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain organized design and asset documentation for Data Center electrical packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with NFPA 70, 70B, 70E, NESC, and IEEE standards, prioritizing safety and engineering excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in electrical engineering, computer engineering, physics, or another engineering discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of electrical design experience in data center, industrial, or utility facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience producing issued-for-construction drawing sets in AutoCAD, AutoCAD Electrical, or Revit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of NEC Articles 110, 215, 240, 250, 310, and 450.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medium-voltage cable system design experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with power systems analysis software and tools: ETAP, SKM, EasyPower, Matlab, PSCAD, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Revit or BIM coordination experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer in Training certification, or on track for a Professional Engineer license.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience on a repeated, multi-phase build rather than one-off projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated initiative, creative problem-solving, and strong analytical/engineering fundamentals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform hands-on work in all environments (heat, cold, rain), in tight quarters or at heights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work extended hours and weekends as needed to support construction, energization, and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remain focused in hazardous environments while wearing appropriate PPE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lift up to 25 lbs. unassisted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide 24/7 on-call support for emergencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to work on-site in Memphis, TN. This is not a remote or hybrid role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel up to 25% for factory witness testing, vendor and OEM engagement, and supporting other sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver&#39;s license.&lt;/li&gt;
