&lt;p&gt;The Director, Memphis Power Plant Operations provides strategic and operational leadership for the gas turbine power generation facility supporting SpaceXSI&#39;s Colossus data center campus in Memphis, Tennessee. This role oversees all plant operations, maintenance, commissioning, and continued construction/expansion of the dedicated power plant, with full ownership of delivering reliable, high-availability electrical power to the Colossus AI training clusters. The position is responsible for driving operational excellence, ensuring 24/7 power reliability and quality, safety, environmental compliance, and leading cross-functional teams to achieve aggressive scale-up, availability, cost, and schedule objectives in a high-growth, fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic and operational leadership for the Memphis gas turbine power plant, including 24/7 operations, maintenance, commissioning, and ongoing construction and capacity expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end delivery of electrical power to the Colossus data center sites, ensuring industry-leading reliability, availability, power quality, and redundancy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multidisciplinary teams of operators, maintenance technicians, engineers, contractors, and support staff in a 24/7 operational and construction environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee plant performance, commissioning, testing, and seamless integration with data center electrical infrastructure and load&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute comprehensive operations and maintenance strategies, including preventative/predictive maintenance, outage planning, hot gas path management, and OEM coordination for gas turbines, generators, balance of plant, and high-voltage electrical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage concurrent construction, equipment installation, civil works, and phased capacity expansions while maintaining safe, reliable operation of the existing plant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure full compliance with environmental, safety, and regulatory requirements, including air permits, emissions controls, TDEC, EPA, OSHA, and local authorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with SpaceXSI data center operations, engineering, fuel suppliers, OEMs, utilities, and regulatory agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formulate and execute operating budgets, fuel management, O&amp;amp;M, capital projects, and annual operating plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement in plant availability, heat rate, emissions, cost, safety metrics, and operational processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and promote a culture of uncompromising safety, accountability, operational excellence, rapid execution, and collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the site leader and primary representative to the Memphis community, regulators, and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop, coach, and retain high-performing talent; manage staffing, resource allocation, and contractor oversight for both operations and construction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in mechanical, electrical, or other engineering discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in power generation operations, plant management, or related industrial or aerospace operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of leadership experience managing teams of operators, technicians, and engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating or managing gas turbine power plants (simple cycle or combined cycle)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing large-scale gas turbine facilities (100 MW+), preferably with high-availability critical power applications (data centers, industrial, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of achieving and sustaining high plant availability, reliability, and low forced outage rates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with plant construction, commissioning, start-up, and concurrent operations/expansion of gas turbine facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of gas turbine technology (aeroderivative and/or heavy-duty frames), performance optimization, emissions controls (SCR, etc.), and balance of plant systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-voltage electrical systems, generators, switchgear, protection, and data center or industrial interconnection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of environmental permitting, air quality compliance, and regulatory reporting for combustion turbines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fast-paced, high-growth environments requiring simultaneous operations and major construction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage budgets, fuel costs, contractors, and complex stakeholder relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent oral and written communication, leadership, and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unfazed by major, abrupt changes in strategic direction or aggressive timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a demanding, autonomously driven, start-up atmosphere&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to support and supervise plant operations and construction outside of normal business hours, including nights, weekends, and on-call response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be based at the Memphis, TN site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work extended hours as needed to support plant reliability and construction milestones&lt;/li&gt;
