&lt;p&gt;The Power Generation team is seeking an Electrical Technician to operate and maintain plant electrical systems at SpaceXSI&#39;s power generation facility. You will work hands-on across medium-voltage generation, distribution, and balance-of-plant electrical equipment up to 13.5 kV and 34.8 kV. This is an operations and maintenance role — you will switch, troubleshoot, repair, and keep electrical systems online in a high-reliability, fast-paced plant environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform operations and maintenance on plant electrical systems, including generators, transformers, switchgear, motor control centers, motors, VFDs, UPS units, automatic transfer switches, and emergency/black-start equipment, at voltages up to 13.5 kV and 34.8 kV.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute switching, isolation, LOTO, racking of breakers, and restoration of medium-voltage equipment in accordance with plant procedures and NFPA 70E.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot electrical faults on power distribution, protection, grounding, lighting, and auxiliary systems using one-line diagrams, schematics, and electrical test equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform preventive and predictive maintenance, inspections, and repairs to improve reliability and reduce unplanned downtime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support plant startups, shutdowns, outages, and commissioning activities alongside operators, controls technicians, and engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install, terminate, and maintain plant electrical equipment, cable, and control wiring as required for operations and maintenance work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to electrical alarms, trips, and equipment failures; support root-cause investigations and implement corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with operations, engineering, and utility personnel on switching, clearances, and electrical work that affects plant generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate work orders, switching records, and as-found/as-left documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow all safety, LOTO, arc-flash, and PPE requirements while working in energized and hazardous plant environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience as an electrical technician, industrial electrician, or similar role maintaining industrial or power generation electrical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating and maintaining medium-voltage electrical systems (4.16 kV to 34.8 kV), including switchgear, transformers, and breakers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a power plant, generating station, or other high-reliability industrial facility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret single-line diagrams, electrical schematics, and equipment O&amp;amp;M manuals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with LOTO, switching procedures, and NFPA 70E / arc-flash safety practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience troubleshooting motors, VFDs, MCCs, UPS systems, and plant auxiliary electrical equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with electrical test equipment (multimeters, insulation testers, infrared, and similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Journeyman electrician license or equivalent formal electrical training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using a CMMS or work-order system to plan and close maintenance work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and as part of a multi-discipline operations and maintenance team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to perform hands-on work in all environments (heat, cold, rain), in tight quarters or at heights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work extended hours, nights, weekends, and rotating or on-call schedules to support plant operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to remain focused in hazardous environments while wearing appropriate PPE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 25 lbs. unassisted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifting, standing, climbing, bending, grasping, sitting, pulling, pushing, stooping, stretching, and carrying are generally required to perform the functions of this position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work on-site at the power generation facility, with potential travel to other SpaceX sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Construction Electrician, you will install and terminate new electrical infrastructure: conduit, cable tray, underground duct bank, cable, wire, and 480 V building and feeder work. This is a build job, not an operating-plant job — pull, land, and energize new equipment from drawings, then turn it over. You will follow lockout/tagout and grounding procedures and support first energization of new 480 V systems. This position is based in Southaven, MS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an hourly position with overtime. Expect 80% or more travel on a rotation, with per diem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install, terminate, and land new campus electrical equipment, including breakers, transformers, switches, buswork, control systems, and batteries at 480 V.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install conduit, cable tray, cable, wire, and terminations per issued-for-construction drawings; perform underground duct bank, trench, and cable-pull work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform installation quality checks and electrical testing (voltmeters, ohmmeters, ammeters, insulation megger) and assist with acceptance and commissioning tests on new gear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read and interpret construction drawings, one-lines, schematics, wiring diagrams, and work orders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow lockout/tagout (LOTO), grounding, clearance procedures, NFPA 70E, and PPE requirements on an active construction site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uncrate, set, and dress equipment; climb structures; operate hand and power tools, pulls, blowers, pumps, and portable generators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support construction energization sequences, punch-list closeout, and turnover to operations with engineers and vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document work performed, test results, and as-built markups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate company vehicles and specialized equipment; inspect and store personal protective equipment (PPE).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform similar or less skilled incidental duties as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current state journeyman electrician license (Tennessee or Mississippi preferred, or equivalent state journeyman license with the ability to obtain TN or MS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of industrial or data center electrical construction installing conduit, tray, duct bank, cable, and 480 V terminations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read construction drawings, one-lines, manuals, and work packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with common electrical test tools (multimeter, megger, ammeter) and construction hand and power tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of NFPA 70E and lockout/tagout (LOTO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift 50+ lbs, work at heights and in confined spaces, and work outdoors in all weather.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hourly position with overtime; willingness to work nights, weekends, and extended shifts during construction and energization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and willingness to travel 80% or more on a construction rotation; per diem and/or housing provided while on site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tennessee or Mississippi journeyman electrician license.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industrial, manufacturing, or data center construction experience building raceway and cable plant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience on large-scale, multi-site construction projects that required a travel rotation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OSHA 30 or equivalent construction safety training in addition to NFPA 70E.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of print reading for drawings, manuals, and one-lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule varies depending on site operational needs; frequent overtime and weekend support is required.&lt;/li&gt;
