&lt;p&gt;As a Construction Electrician, you will install and terminate new electrical infrastructure: conduit, cable tray, underground duct bank, cable, wire, and 480 V building and feeder work. This is a build job, not an operating-plant job — pull, land, and energize new equipment from drawings, then turn it over. You will follow lockout/tagout (LOTO) and grounding procedures and support first energization of new 480 V systems. This position is primarily based in Southaven, MS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install, terminate, and land new campus electrical equipment, including breakers, transformers, switches, buswork, control systems, and batteries at 480 V&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install conduit, cable tray, cable, wire, and terminations per issued-for-construction drawings; perform underground duct bank, trench, and cable-pull work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform installation quality checks and electrical testing (voltmeters, ohmmeters, ammeters, insulation megger) and assist with acceptance and commissioning tests on new gear&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read and interpret construction drawings, one-lines, schematics, wiring diagrams, and work orders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow lockout/tagout (LOTO), grounding, clearance procedures, NFPA 70E, and PPE requirements on an active construction site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uncrate, set, and dress equipment; climb structures; operate hand and power tools, pulls, blowers, pumps, and portable generators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support construction energization sequences, punch-list closeout, and turnover to operations with engineers and vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document work performed, test results, and as-built markups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate company vehicles and specialized equipment; inspect and store personal protective equipment (PPE)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform similar or less skilled incidental duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of industrial or data center electrical construction installing conduit, tray, duct bank, cable, and 480 V terminations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read construction drawings, one-lines, manuals, and work packages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with common electrical test tools (multimeter, megger, ammeter) and construction hand and power tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of NFPA 70E and lockout/tagout (LOTO)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current state journeyman electrician license (Tennessee or Mississippi preferred, or equivalent state journeyman license with the ability to obtain TN or MS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industrial, manufacturing, or data center construction experience building raceway and cable plant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience on large-scale, multi-site construction projects that required a travel rotation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OSHA 30 or equivalent construction safety training in addition to NFPA 70E&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of print reading for drawings, manuals, and one-lines&lt;/li&gt;
