&lt;p&gt;As a Facilities Maintenance Assistant at SpaceXSI Memphis, you will support the upkeep of our supercomputing data center facilities by assisting with routine non-critical maintenance tasks. Under close supervision, you&#39;ll help with basic operations and limited maintenance on critical equipment, contributing to a reliable and efficient environment that powers our AI-driven mission. This entry-level role emphasizes hands-on learning, teamwork, and attention to detail in a fast-paced setting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in performing non-critical maintenance and repair work, including people door repairs, administrative area upkeep, building envelope maintenance, and/or landscaping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Under direct supervision of an operator, assist as required in the operation of critical equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the performance of limited maintenance on offline critical equipment as directed, including: single chiller maintenance, single CDU filter changeouts, and/or leak detection verification in alarming racks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support daily inspections of facilities areas to identify and report potential issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help maintain spare parts inventory and assist with basic organization of tools and equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow standard operating procedures (SOPs) and safety protocols during all tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with team members to ensure timely completion of maintenance activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support during scheduled system maintenance or minor repairs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in documenting work performed and any observed issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in team training sessions and contribute to a collaborative work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
