&lt;p&gt;As a Fiber Technician at SpaceXSI&#39;s data center, you’ll dive into the world of fiber optic systems, applying your core skills and eagerness to grow in a high-growth tech environment. Working onsite with passionate teams, you’ll tackle hands-on challenges to install and maintain critical network infrastructure, ensuring seamless connectivity. Expect to collaborate closely, refine your expertise, and keep our systems running smoothly to support SpaceXSI&#39;s mission of accelerating human scientific discovery through AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Under the guidance of the Foreman Supervisor, Project Manager, and Superintendent manage all phases of data center installation projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a safe and productive work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop sensor indicators and conduct timely inspections, so that a faulty fiber optic system does not destabilize its performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot, resolve, repair and install fiber optics systems, ensuring that they work properly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Examine and replace faulty and/or old fiber optic cables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize scheduled maintenance routines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take care of fiber splicing and rectify fiber optic problem areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep track of the signal strength of different devices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formulate and maintain system records and system designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of direct data center experience installing and routing optical fiber in large scale Tier 3 or 4 facilities as a commercial fiber optic technician&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification in fiber optics and/or cable installation&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience in fiber splicing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical knowledge of communication networks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledgeable of computers and associated electronic systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledgeable of different fiber types&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience installing, certifying, and troubleshooting fiber in hyperscale data center environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience installing structured cabling&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly proficient using a light meter, OTDR (Optical Time Domain Reflectometer), OPMs (optical power meter), fiber certifier, loopback, and optical probes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to understand different types of switches and port identifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to properly clean fiber and validate cleanliness&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position is subject to pre-employment drug and random drug and alcohol testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position is subject to pre-employment and annual post employment background checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work is often performed in tight quarters and physical dexterity is necessary to perform job functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 35 lbs unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working at elevated heights (up to 50 feet) with appropriate safety gear&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in an environment requiring exposure to noise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available to work evenings and weekends, as the schedule varies depending on site operational needs; flexibility is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

