&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalent certificate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional experience working with HVAC, plumbing, pneumatic, mechanical, or electrical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge in the following areas: HVAC, plumbing, electrical safety, pneumatic principles, tubing, pipefittings, rotating machinery (pumps, air compressors, etc.), and a variety of mechanical fasteners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical certification, journeyman, or master in HVAC, mechanical, plumbing, or electrical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of high-pressure gas, flammable gas, and refrigeration gases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional experience maintaining high efficiency particulate air (HEPA) filters and standard air handling unit (AHU) filtration systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to troubleshoot mechanical and electrical systems down to the component level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with commercial building codes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read, interpret, and understand technical language in specifications, schematics, and blueprints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use Microsoft Word, Excel, and PowerPoint to generate service reports and communicate within the company including skills to navigate web-based service literature and programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possesses a good attitude, willingness to learn, flexibility, and is a self-starter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates a consistent record of punctual schedule adherence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in a high-stress environment balancing several projects at any given time and the flexibility to adjust for abrupt changes in strategic direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an Industrial Pipefitter to support the buildout of SpaceXSI&#39;s high-performance data centers. In this hands-on role, you will install large industrial piping systems and keep construction moving on our next-generation AI supercomputing infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with mechanical, welding, structural, electrical, and operations teams to fit, hang, and test pipe from construction through turnover. This is a full-time, onsite role with significant travel to SpaceXSI data center sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install large-bore industrial piping (process, mechanical, utility, and related systems): measure, cut, bevel, fit, hang, and make up joints per drawings and specs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform flange, groove, thread, and welded-joint fit-up; align pipe, set gaps, and prep joints for the welding crew.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install valves, fittings, hangers, supports, strut, and anchors; hang pipe racks and supports plumb and on grade.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read isometric, spool, and arrangement drawings; field-route as directed and flag drawing conflicts before install.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support hydro, pneumatic, and service tests: install blinds and test packs, walk lines, and repair leaks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stage, move, and inventory pipe, valves, hangers, insulation, tools, and equipment; keep laydown yards and mechanical rooms orderly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with equipment set for pumps, cooling towers, air handlers, and related mechanical gear, including bolt-up of suction and discharge piping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open and close work areas: protection, debris removal, scrap segregation, and end-of-shift reset so the next crew can start immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow LOTO, PPE, and permit rules; do not work on live systems without authorization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report damaged material, unsafe conditions, and drawing conflicts immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support punch-list work and cleanup through system turnover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years installing large industrial or commercial piping OR completion of a recognized pipefitter apprenticeship, OR equivalent military experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience fitting and installing welded, flanged, grooved, and/or threaded pipe, including hangers and supports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work at heights, outdoors, and on a changing data center construction site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use pipefitting hand tools, power tools, bevelers, and material-handling equipment safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong safety mindset and willingness to follow site procedures, including LOTO and permits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work extended hours, nights, and weekends during critical construction windows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience on data center, industrial, or heavy-civil construction sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience on large-bore welded industrial piping (carbon and/or stainless) and equipment connections (pumps, air handlers, cooling towers, skids).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read isometric, spool, and P&amp;amp;ID drawings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UA, NCCER, or equivalent pipefitter credential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OSHA 10 or equivalent training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with hot-work, hydrotest, and flange-management practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel extensively to SpaceXSI data center construction sites and remain onsite during peak construction phases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capability to work in industrial environments, climb ladders, lift and position moderate loads, stand and walk for a full shift, and wear PPE for extended periods, with or without reasonable accommodation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an Industrial Welder to support the buildout of SpaceXSI&#39;s high-performance data centers. In this hands-on role, you will fit and weld large industrial piping and structural steel to ASME Section IX and keep construction moving on our next-generation AI supercomputing infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with mechanical, structural, electrical, and operations teams to weld pipe, supports, and structures from construction through turnover. This is a full-time, onsite role with significant travel to SpaceXSI data center sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fit, tack, and weld large-bore industrial piping and/or structural steel (pipe racks, platforms, supports, skids, and related assemblies) per drawings and ASME Section IX welding procedure specifications (WPS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lay out, cut, bevel, grind, and align joints; check fit-up, root opening, and reinforcement before and after the weld.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read isometric, spool, and structural drawings; work to weld maps, heat numbers, and rod-control / continuity requirements where used.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support hanging of strut, supports, hangers, and structural members; assist with equipment set and bolt-up as needed to complete the weld package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stage, move, and inventory pipe, fittings, structural members, filler metal, and tools; keep laydown yards and work areas orderly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open and close work areas: protection, fire watch and hot-work permits, debris removal, scrap segregation, and end-of-shift reset so the next crew can start immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow LOTO, PPE, hot-work, and site rules; do not weld on live or unpurged systems without authorization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report damaged material, rejected welds, unsafe conditions, and drawing conflicts immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support punch-list, repair, and NDE hold-point work through system turnover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Journey-level industrial construction welding experience: 3+ years welding large industrial piping and/or structural steel, completion of a recognized welding apprenticeship, or equivalent military experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with GTAW (TIG) on stainless steel and/or SMAW (stick) on carbon steel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified to ASME Section IX, or ability to pass a pre-employment weld test to ASME Section IX in the process(es) and position(s) used on site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work at heights, outdoors, and on a changing data center construction site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use welding machines, torches, grinders, and related hand and power tools safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong safety mindset and willingness to follow site procedures, including hot-work permits and LOTO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience on data center, industrial, or heavy-civil construction sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience welding large-bore process, mechanical, or utility piping and heavy structural members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current ASME Section IX qualification (e.g. 6G) in GTAW on stainless and/or SMAW on carbon.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in both TIG-on-stainless and stick-on-carbon; FCAW a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS D1.1 structural welding qualification or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OSHA 10 or equivalent training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read isometric, spool, and structural drawings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel extensively to SpaceXSI data center construction sites and remain onsite during peak construction phases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capability to work in industrial environments, climb ladders, lift and position moderate loads, stand and walk for a full shift, and wear PPE (including welding PPE) for extended periods, with or without reasonable accommodation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;INFRASTRUCTURE SECURITY ENGINEER, BARE METAL &amp;amp; PLATFORM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a hands-on Infrastructure Security Engineer to build and secure SpaceXSI&#39;s infrastructure from the bare-metal layer up through the platform and application stack. In this role, you will design, implement, and harden physical and private-cloud foundations—servers, networks, identity, and orchestration—and carry that security posture into containers, automation, and hybrid connectivity with public cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role focuses on securing critical infrastructure spanning data centers, colo, and hybrid environments, with work that may span platforms such as SpaceXSI, X Social, X Money, and related systems. You’ll operate with an automation-first mindset: building secure foundations at the metal and OS layer, hardening platforms at scale, and partnering closely with engineering so security is embedded in how we build and run systems—not bolted on after the fact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Bare metal, data center &amp;amp; network security&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement secure bare-metal and private-cloud architectures (servers, storage, out-of-band management, BIOS/UEFI/BMC firmware posture)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Harden physical and virtual fleets: OS baselines (Linux/Windows), CIS benchmarks, patch and vulnerability management, and secure boot / measured boot where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on firmware, BMC/iDRAC/iLO, PXE/Kickstart provisioning, and hardware lifecycle security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and secure network foundations: segmentation, load balancers, DNS, PKI, NAC, and IDS/IPS on real hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own hybrid connectivity between on-premises and cloud (site-to-site VPN, Direct Connect / Interconnect / ExpressRoute, SD-WAN, zero-trust access)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage identities and privileged access across Active Directory / LDAP / Kerberos and cloud IAM (federation, SAML/OIDC, PAM)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with security assessments and audits of physical, on-premises, and hybrid infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and remediate infrastructure to comply with regulations and best practices (e.g., PCI, NIST CSF, GDPR, HIPAA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Platform, containers &amp;amp; developer enablement&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement secure container and Kubernetes standards on bare metal and private cloud (not only managed EKS/GKE/AKS), including RBAC, network policy, and secrets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain Infrastructure as Code and configuration management—especially Puppet—with embedded security controls for physical and virtual fleets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with development teams so security best practices are integrated into CI/CD pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure and enhance CI/CD pipelines; integrate and maintain code and image scanning platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Detection, operations &amp;amp; tooling&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and respond to security events and incidents spanning bare metal, network devices, hosts, and hybrid cloud&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain SIEM data pipelines that ingest on-premises network, host, and cloud telemetry for reliable alerting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, deploy, and maintain security operations infrastructure using Python, Terraform, and Puppet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop dashboards and alerts from security metrics across physical and platform layers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain infrastructure security policies, standards, and procedures from metal through platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own security projects end to end: identify issues and implement solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current with emerging threats and mitigations for bare-metal, firmware, network, and hybrid-cloud infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in computer science, cybersecurity, or other scientific discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in infrastructure security, platform security, or other hands-on security roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience securing bare-metal, data-center, or private-cloud environments (not cloud-only resumes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience securing AI/ML and GPU workloads on bare metal or hybrid infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with firmware, BMC/iDRAC/iLO, PXE/Kickstart provisioning, and hardware lifecycle security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with Puppet for configuration management and fleet hardening in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of network security concepts and protocols, including hands-on work with firewalls, segmentation, and hybrid connectivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with hybrid identity (AD/LDAP or similar) integrated or federated with cloud IAM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Infrastructure as Code (e.g., Terraform) applied to physical or VM fleets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with languages (e.g., Python, Bash and Golang) for automation and tool development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with containerization and Kubernetes security implications, including on-premises or bare-metal clusters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with regulatory compliance requirements (e.g., GDPR, HIPAA, PCI DSS, NIST CSF)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in banking, money transmission, P2P payments, or similarly regulated financial platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive mindset with strong ownership, critical thinking, and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise operating and securing physical server fleets, colo, or private cloud (VMware, OpenStack, Proxmox, Nutanix, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant security certifications (e.g., CCSP, CSSK, OSCP, network or cloud security specialty)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with Python and Terraform on production fleets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in Kubernetes and container security on bare metal or private cloud&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multi-cloud and cloud-to-on-prem security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of CI/CD best practices and tools; hands-on GitHub Actions or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with observability and security operations tooling (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana, CloudWatch, Karma; SIEM platforms such as Wazuh)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building custom security tools or integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in leveraging AI for infrastructure security monitoring and automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to open-source infrastructure or security projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
