&lt;h3&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive, store, and issue raw material, parts, details, and hardware to support data center construction, commissioning, and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Store parts and materials in designated locations (bins, racks, VLMs, or staging areas), accurately identifying parts and locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strict material handling practices in accordance with procedures, especially for high-value or sensitive equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform picking and kitting functions to assemble necessary kits of parts, material, and hardware; verify all items are available and accounted for&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify all material received for conformity with accompanying paperwork, checking for damage, correct part numbers, quantities, and revisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Issue material against approved paperwork, including affixing verification and maintaining lot/serial traceability as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform cycle counts and maintain high inventory accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Abide by all procedures, work instructions, and standard operating documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage schedule priorities and independently execute work to meet site deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform good housekeeping in inventory and staging areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support material flow, including staging and just-in-time delivery to internal customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of inventory control experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of inventory control experience in a warehouse or distribution environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and understanding of inventory, kitting, and material handling processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating a forklift and other inventory/material handling equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent computer skills, including Microsoft Office (especially Excel)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in aerospace, automotive, semiconductor, electronics, technology, or data center environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret drawings, procedures, and parts lists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ERP/WMS system experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in logistics or supply chain management (preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 25–50 lbs. unassisted; frequent lifting, standing, climbing, bending, grasping, sitting, pulling, pushing, stooping, stretching, and carrying required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be available for one of the following 12.5-hour shifts: 6:00 AM – 6:30 PM or 6:00 PM – 6:30 AM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work schedule follows a rotating pattern of 4 days on / 3 days off, then 3 days on / 4 days off (and repeating)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be open to working all required shift hours, including nights, weekends, overtime, and holidays as needed to support 24/7 operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in warehouse/data center environments with varying temperatures and noise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a skilled Iron Worker to support the buildout of SpaceXSI&#39;s high-performance data centers and AI supercomputing campuses. In this hands-on role, you will erect structural steel, miscellaneous metals, and equipment supports that form the backbone of our next-generation supercomputer halls, cooling plants, substations, and site infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with civil, mechanical, electrical, and operations teams to install the steel that carries buildings, pipe racks, cable tray, busway, cooling equipment, and access systems from foundations through turnover. This is a full-time, onsite role with significant travel to SpaceXSI data center sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Erect structural steel for supercomputer halls, mechanical plants, substations, cooling yards, and site buildings, including columns, beams, bracing, joists, and metal deck.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install miscellaneous metals: stairs, ladders, platforms, catwalks, grating, handrail, embeds, and equipment frames that support construction, operations, and maintenance access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fabricate and install pipe racks, aerial galleries, mezzanines, and support steel for chilled-water piping, cable tray, busway, and liquid-cooling distribution serving AI compute halls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rig, hoist, and set structural members and heavy equipment-support steel using cranes, come-alongs, chain falls, and approved lifting gear; act as rigger or signal person when qualified.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bolt, torque, weld, and plumb connections to drawings, AISC and AWS standards, and inspection requirements; install high-strength bolts and close connection punch lists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read structural drawings, erection plans, and shop drawings; lay out from control, check elevations and plumb, and report conflicts before steel goes up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with civil, mechanical, and electrical crews so embeds, penetrations, and support steel land correctly for cooling towers, generators, transformers, pumps, CDUs, and IT equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow fall protection, crane, rigging, hot-work, LOTO, PPE, and permit rules; keep a safe work area at height and around live construction and energized yards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support inspection, punch-list, and turnover work through building and yard completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of ironworking experience on commercial, industrial, or heavy-civil structural steel, or equivalent military structural or rigging experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read structural and erection drawings and work to AISC connection details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on proficiency with structural bolt-up, cutting, and safe use of aerial lifts, ladders, and material-handling equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work at heights, outdoors, and on a changing construction site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong safety mindset with current OSHA 10 or equivalent training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work extended hours, nights, and weekends during critical construction windows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Journey-level ironworker experience (union or non-union) and/or completion of an ironworker apprenticeship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS D1.1 structural welding certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified rigger and/or signal person; NCCCO or equivalent crane, rigger, or signal certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OSHA 30 and/or fall-protection competent person.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience on hyperscale data center, power plant, industrial, or other mission-critical steel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with pipe rack, equipment support steel, and miscellaneous metals in addition to building steel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel extensively to SpaceXSI construction sites and remain onsite during peak construction phases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capability to work in industrial environments, climb ladders and structural steel, lift moderate to heavy loads, stand and walk for a full shift, and wear PPE for extended periods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work at elevation in varying weather, around cranes and heavy equipment, and in active construction yards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IT NETWORK ENGINEER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceXSI is looking for an experienced network engineer with expertise in networking technologies that support routing, switching, dynamic multicast, Wi-Fi, network access control, automation, etc. This position will be directly involved with supporting and expanding our campus and data center infrastructure as well as our expansive wireless network using reliable and redundant design standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design, implementation, and troubleshooting of large-scale, complex wired and wireless networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure, install, and support campus and data center networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot wired/wireless networking-related issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the deployment of network access control (NAC) using 802.1X&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and enforce network policies and standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and prepare project roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop network automation tools to support our enterprise network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor network health using in-house and third-party tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain proper documentation of our networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in computer science, computer engineering, or other STEM discipline and 2+ years of professional network engineering experience; OR 5+ years of professional network engineering experience in lieu of a degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert understanding of the OSI model and network standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cisco Catalyst, Juniper, and Arista data center-class switches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cisco wireless LAN controllers or other wireless technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network Access Control (NAC) using 802.1X&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wave Division Multiplexing and Fiber Optics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DNS, DHCP, SNMP, IP helpers, ARP, CDP, LLDP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BGP routing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Switch port security features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network monitoring tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Linux/Windows system administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python scripting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry-standard certifications such as CCNP, CCIE, JNCIP, or JNCIE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be available to work extended hours and weekends as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role requires you to be onsite – hybrid or remote work will not be considered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have a valid driver&#39;s license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our IT Services team is the backbone of our operational efficiency, ensuring seamless connectivity and technical assistance for all our employees, regardless of their location. We are seeking a skilled and helpful IT specialist to join our IT services team. This role provides advanced technical guidance and service to end-users, resolves complex IT issues, and collaborates with Level 1 technicians and senior IT staff to ensure seamless technology operations. The ideal candidate is a problem-solver with strong technical expertise, excellent communication skills, and a commitment to delivering outstanding customer service. This is a full-time position, onsite with occasional on-call or after-hours support.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide second-line technical assistance for hardware, software, and network issues via phone, email, or in-person.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose and resolve complex technical problems, including system crashes, network connectivity issues, and software conflicts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and administer user accounts, permissions, and access controls in systems like Active Directory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the deployment, configuration, and maintenance of hardware (desktops, laptops, servers, and peripherals) and software applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and maintain IT systems, including performing patch management, updates, and basic server administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document and update IT service tickets with detailed resolutions and escalate unresolved issues to Level 3 experts or specialized teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to and maintain IT knowledge base articles and self-service wikis to enhance user self-sufficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support IT projects, such as system upgrades, migrations, or new technology rollouts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train and mentor Level 1 technicians, providing guidance on troubleshooting techniques and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with company IT policies, security standards, and data protection protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide new hire onboarding and offboarding service support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate’s or Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or a related field preferred; equivalent experience considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-4 years of experience in IT, helpdesk, or a related technical role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of Windows and macOS operating systems, Microsoft Office Suite, and common enterprise software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in troubleshooting network issues (TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, VPNs) and basic server administration (Windows Server, Linux basics).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with IT service management tools (e.g., ServiceNow, Jira) and ticketing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with virtualization technologies (e.g., VMware, Hyper-V) and cloud services (e.g., Google Workspace, Microsoft 365) is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving, analytical, and customer service skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certifications (e.g., CompTIA A+, Network+, Microsoft Certified Professional, or ITIL) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with scripting (e.g., PowerShell, Bash,Python) for automation tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of cybersecurity best practices and tools (e.g., antivirus, endpoint protection).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
