&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the High Power Engineering team supporting SpaceXSI to design, build, operate, and maintain electrical infrastructure for AI training campuses. As a Lead Engineer for Transmission &amp;amp; Distribution, you will work with a small on-site team to scale high-capacity power systems on a schedule set by compute demand. The position is based in Memphis, TN, with potential travel to other sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own everything from generation terminals and the point of interconnection down to the medium-voltage bus: high-voltage switchyards, collector transmission, main power transformers, and the utility relationship that determines whether the campus energizes on schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own high-voltage switchyard architecture: bus configuration, GIS versus AIS tradeoffs, bus sectionalizing, and fault-current management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the interconnection process with the local distributor and balancing authority, including application, system impact and facilities studies, protection philosophy alignment, telemetry and metering, and technical exhibits to the service agreement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own campus protection philosophy and the settings management database served to Data Center and Battery Storage — one owner, not three models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the campus power systems studies function: the single model of record for load flow, short circuit, coordination, arc flash, and stability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the generation electrical interface: excitation and governor behavior, synchronizing, generator protection, black start, and station service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own regulatory and compliance scope as assigned: service agreements, applicable NERC/SERC standards, air-permitting coordination, AHJ relationships, and compliance evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the campus electrical safety program: NFPA 70E, arc-flash study currency and labeling, energized work permitting, qualified-worker training, and switching authorization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct Design, Ops/Build, Protection &amp;amp; Controls, and Power System Engineer seats on the T&amp;amp;D team as those seats fill.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in electrical engineering, computer engineering, physics, or another engineering discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in transmission, substation, or generation interconnection engineering, with a focus on high-power, high-voltage systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience carrying a project through utility or ISO interconnection to energization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCES:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional Engineering license or intention to actively seek a PE license.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of the IEEE C37 series, IEEE 80, NESC, and applicable NERC standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;161 kV, 230 kV, or 345 kV GIS or AIS experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Large-load interconnection experience with TVA, MLGW, or comparable municipal or federal power arrangements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with power systems analysis software and tools: ETAP, SKM, PSS/E, PSCAD, ASPEN, Matlab, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a multidisciplinary engineering team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead teams, work independently, and thrive in dynamic, high-stress environments with tight deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform hands-on work in all environments (heat, cold, rain), in tight quarters or at heights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work extended hours and weekends as needed to support construction, energization, and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remain focused in hazardous environments while wearing appropriate PPE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lift up to 25 lbs. unassisted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide 24/7 on-call support for emergencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to work on-site in Memphis, TN. This is not a remote or hybrid role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel up to 25% for factory witness testing, vendor and OEM engagement, and supporting other sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver&#39;s license.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LEAD FIBER TECHNICIAN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Lead Fiber Technician on SpaceXSI&#39;s traveling data center build team, you will lead crews in the installation, testing, and commissioning of high-performance fiber optic infrastructure across multiple new and expanding data center sites. You’ll bring strong leadership, technical expertise, and a safety-first mindset to fast-paced hyperscale construction projects. This role involves significant travel to support greenfield and expansion builds, ensuring reliable, high-speed network connectivity that powers SpaceXSI&#39;s AI training clusters. You will mentor technicians, drive execution excellence, and help deliver mission-critical infrastructure on aggressive timelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as crew leader for traveling fiber teams, managing daily work assignments, resource allocation, and execution based on Fiber Span sheets, site surveys, path planning, and cross-functional coordination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and mentor a team of Fiber Technicians across multiple project sites, providing on-the-job training, technical guidance, and performance feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee all phases of fiber optic installation projects from planning and mobilization through execution, testing, handover, and closeout at new data center builds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a safe, productive, high-quality, and compliant work environment in dynamic construction settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and monitor sensor indicators; conduct timely inspections and quality checks to prevent system issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot, resolve, repair, and install complex fiber optics systems in both OSP and ISP environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead fiber splicing (fusion and mechanical), termination, labeling, and certification activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Examine, replace, and optimize faulty or aging fiber optic cables and infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize scheduled maintenance, testing routines, and documentation during build phases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor signal strength, attenuation, and overall network performance; maintain detailed system records, as-built drawings, and designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate closely with superintendents, project managers, other trades (electrical, mechanical, controls), and GC teams to align with overall data center construction schedules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support site mobilization/demobilization, tool/equipment management, and knowledge transfer between projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of direct experience in fiber optic installation, splicing, and testing in large-scale data center or critical infrastructure environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years in a foreman, crew lead, or supervisory role leading fiber/cabling teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in Tier 3/4 or hyperscale environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience working on traveling or multi-site construction/build projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on knowledge of fiber optic best practices, OTDR/power meter testing, structured cabling, and safety protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification in fiber optics and/or cable installation (e.g., FOA, BICSI, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience with fusion splicing, high-density fiber deployments, and hyperscale/AI/HPC data center environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical knowledge of communication networks, different fiber types (single-mode, multi-mode, etc.), and associated systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in data center greenfield construction or rapid deployment projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating with general contractors and multi-trade teams in fast-paced builds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with project documentation, digital tools, and quality assurance processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to travel extensively (typically 50-75% or more, depending on project needs) to SpaceXSI data center construction sites across the US, with potential for extended stays at project locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in tight quarters, at elevated heights (up to 50 feet with proper safety gear), and in active construction environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 35 lbs unassisted and maintain physical dexterity for installation tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in high-noise environments and varying weather conditions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to work evenings, weekends, and extended hours as dictated by project schedules and deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver’s license and clean driving record (company vehicle or travel support provided)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Lead, Inventory Specialist at SpaceXSI, you will oversee warehouse and inventory operations supporting our rapidly expanding data centers. You will lead the receiving, storage, kitting, issuance, and tracking of high-value servers, networking equipment, power and cooling components, spare parts, and infrastructure materials. In this role you will mentor team members, manage daily priorities and backlogs, drive inventory accuracy, and ensure material is available when needed for construction, commissioning, and ongoing operations. You are expected to be hands-on, maintain a high sense of urgency, and continuously improve processes in a fast-paced, high-growth environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support daily/weekly team meetings by participating in ways to help the team improve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee daily shift backlogs and inventory-related queues. Maintain continual oversight of incoming receipts, RMA backlogs, and outgoing material requests to ensure compliance with metric targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Re-assign daily shift resources to meet demands and prioritize critical data center hardware, spare parts, and infrastructure materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide input to employees’ performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Function as focal point for area group production coordinators, Site Operations, and priorities related to inventory and material flow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in adding to the area’s to-do lists for improvement projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fulfill resource gaps when shifts are short-handed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor employees to meet supervisor expectations for the job&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train continuously to improve the workers’ skills in inventory accuracy, material handling, and system processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor department consumables, spare parts, and critical inventory levels; drive reordering and replenishment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the general inventory/fulfillment email inbox and resolve issues promptly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive, inspect, store, and issue servers, networking gear, power/cooling components, parts, details, and hardware as required to support data center construction, expansion, and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Store parts and materials in bins, drawers, racks, and designated locations; accurately identify part numbers and storage locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform picking functions to make up necessary kits of parts, material, and hardware; ascertain that all items are available and accounted for in kit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strict material handling practices in accordance with procedures, especially for high-value and sensitive equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor shelf-life storage and maintain proper rotation of stock (FIFO)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate environmental and temperature requirements for any temperature-sensitive materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with other fulfillment centers, other sites, Shipping, Receiving, Planning, Quality Control, Purchasing, Procurement, and related departments to resolve problems relative to receipt and distribution of material&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain good housekeeping and organization of warehouse and staging areas for efficiency (5S principles)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the organization’s metric goals and objectives for inventory accuracy, cycle count compliance, and material availability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct and oversee regular inventory audits, cycle counts, and reconciliations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Return Merchandise Authorization (RMA) processes, including inspection, documentation, and coordination with vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in a warehouse environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience working in materials management or inventory control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data entry and inventory tracking systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capability to operate a forklift and other related inventory/material handling equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within data center, technology, aerospace, semiconductor, or high-volume manufacturing environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent computer skills including Microsoft Office / Google Workspace (Word, Excel/Sheets, Outlook)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ERP or WMS system experience (SAP, Oracle, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and understanding of inventory, kitting, and RMA processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail oriented, organized, and demonstrates a high sense of urgency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior lead or supervisory experience in warehouse/inventory operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with structured cabling, server/hardware handling, or data center material flow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift 25–50 lbs. unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifting, standing, climbing, bending, grasping, sitting, pulling, pushing, stooping, stretching, and carrying are generally required to perform the functions of this position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work flexible shifts, overtime, and weekends as needed to support data center operations and build schedules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work in a warehouse and data center environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Lead, Receiving Specialist&lt;/strong&gt; to oversee inbound receiving operations supporting data center construction and operations in Memphis, TN. In this working-lead role, you will lead a team of Receiving Specialists in the accurate, timely, and damage-free receipt of high-value materials and equipment (including servers, networking gear, power systems, cooling infrastructure, and other critical components). You will combine hands-on execution with team leadership to maintain inventory integrity, resolve discrepancies, and support aggressive project timelines in a fast-paced, high-growth environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and coordinate a team of Receiving Specialists; assign work, provide training, and ensure consistent, high-quality execution of receiving processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee receipt of all incoming materials and packages; transact receipts in the ERP/WMS system and process hold packages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, print, and apply routing labels and required identifiers; maintain accurate records of incoming paperwork&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify all material received for conformity with accompanying documentation, checking for damage, correct part numbers, and quantity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with carriers, vendors, purchasing, logistics, facilities, and construction/operations teams to resolve receipt, discrepancy, and distribution issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate return shipments and reverse logistics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review stagnant inventory reports and support location accuracy and inventory reconciliation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate forklifts and powered industrial equipment in accordance with safety procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive good housekeeping, 5S, and process improvements to enhance efficiency, accuracy, and safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document non-conformances and support root-cause and corrective-action processes as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in receiving, supply chain, warehouse, or manufacturing environment, including at least 1 year in a lead, senior, or supervisory capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in a receiving role, preferably supporting data center, construction, or high-tech operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ERP or warehouse management systems and scanning equipment (RF/handheld scanners)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating a forklift and other powered industrial equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling high-value or sensitive electronics, servers, or critical infrastructure components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with nonconforming material control, discrepancy resolution, and inventory accuracy processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong computer skills, including Microsoft suite proficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead teams, train others, and drive operational improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be open to working either day shift (6:00 AM – 4:00 PM) or night shift (6:00 PM – 4:00 AM), Monday–Friday, with weekends included when needed to support 24/7 project demands; flexibility to cover overtime as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to stand, walk, bend, stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, and perform physical tasks for extended periods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work in a warehouse environment that may include exposure to varying temperatures, noise, and dust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commitment to safety protocols and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
