&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;job__description body&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceXSI is building and operating one of the world’s most demanding AI training campuses in Memphis, including Colossus and site facilities that support it. The people who work here—and the buildings and grounds they occupy—have to keep up with that tempo. We are looking for a Facilities Manager to oversee operation and maintenance of an assigned portfolio of office and support buildings on that campus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is directly responsible for keeping building systems in top condition, holding maintenance costs down, keeping vendors efficient, and presenting a campus that reflects our standards to employees, visitors, and VIPs. You will lead an internal team and vendors through work orders, preventive maintenance, building HVAC, plumbing, electrical, janitorial, and grounds—the day-to-day care of our facilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our facility care is a direct reflection of our values, and the impact is immense.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a team responsible for facilities maintenance (building operations, janitorial, landscaping/grounds, and general maintenance) for an assigned portfolio of Memphis campus buildings to ensure continual service to employees and visitors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee building HVAC systems, plumbing systems, fire suppression systems, and electrical systems (including basic transformers).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the work ticketing system to ensure correct staffing and timely response to break/fix requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage third-party service providers to ensure services meet corporate standards and terms of contract.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the construction team to develop, plan, and execute site improvement projects in accordance with overall business objectives and strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer an effective and efficient preventive maintenance and break/fix program for the assigned buildings and grounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement on-call after-hours support for facility troubleshooting and emergency repairs (leaks, HVAC, electrical, and related building issues).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach, develop, and hold technicians accountable to safety, quality, and response-time standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep maintenance costs low, vendors competitive, and the appearance and function of assigned buildings at a standard that matches the site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in an engineering, business, or supply chain discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience with facilities engineering or project management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft applications such as Excel, Outlook, Word, and PowerPoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing budgets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing third-party vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating contracts and comparing service costs to achieve maximum value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with asset management or CMMS / work-order software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of building management and automated facilities monitoring systems and processes, such as HVAC systems, plumbing systems, fire suppression systems, generators, or related building equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and cleanliness standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently with little direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to meet deadlines in a fast-paced, ever-changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to anticipate needs and develop innovative solutions for continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading technicians or trades in an office, industrial, or campus environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based at the Memphis, TN campus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work extended hours and/or weekends as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide 24/7 on-call support of critical facility activities and emergency situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a high-tempo environment while balancing multiple priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MANAGER, DATA CENTER OPERATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Data Center Operations Manager, you’ll oversee the data center technicians who keep SpaceXSI&#39;s AI infrastructure running smoothly. This role is pivotal in ensuring our systems operate at peak efficiency, supporting the compute power behind our mission. You’ll co-lead a skilled team, manage critical operations, and implement smart, sustainable solutions. We’re looking for someone with technical expertise and a proactive approach to maintain and scale our facilities effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee site operations by managing power, cooling, networking, and hardware deployments to ensure 99.999% uptime for SpaceXSI&#39;s AI compute systems, keeping our infrastructure reliable and ready for innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a team of Data Center Operations Technicians through training, performance evaluations, and fostering a collaborative, high-performing environment tied to SpaceXSI&#39;s objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Streamline processes by taking charge of hardware lifecycles, incident resolution, and inventory management, refining procedures to ensure your team operates with precision and consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate between technicians, SpaceXSI&#39;s AI specialists, and external vendors to integrate new technology and expand capacity seamlessly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive sustainable solutions by championing energy-efficient practices and sustainability efforts, optimizing resources while supporting the demands of cutting-edge AI workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report key metrics like uptime, power efficiency, and issue resolution times, using data to enhance site performance and inform decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle emergencies and lead the team through urgent situations with clear direction, resolving issues quickly to protect our AI systems from disruption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize operations by building and refining processes—such as preventative maintenance schedules with vendors and ticket workflows in Jira—to keep operations efficient and scalable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with leadership to standardize best practices across sites (if applicable), ensuring operations align with SpaceXSI&#39;s ambitious growth plans to support expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in data center operations or critical environments, with 3+ years managing technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead teams effectively in fast-paced, high-responsibility settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid expertise in server hardware, cabling, and data center technologies, from setup to lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting compute-heavy environments like AI, machine learning, or high-performance computing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with tools like Jira and managing collaborative workflows across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to diverse audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with scripting (e.g., Python, Bash) to automate tasks and boost team efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of partnering with vendors, scaling operations, and advancing sustainability initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiasm for SpaceXSI&#39;s mission to accelerate human discovery and unravel the universe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a dynamic, mission-focused environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to work occasional on-call duties&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel to data center locations as needed to support operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physical capability to handle data center tasks, including lifting up to 50 lbs, standing for long periods, and occasional ladder use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Manager of Engineering to own the design, build-out, commissioning, and continuous improvement of automation, controls, and electrical systems at SpaceXSI&#39;s power generation facility in Southaven. This plant is critical infrastructure for SpaceXSI&#39;s AI supercomputers: it must deliver high-reliability power and supporting utilities at scale, with the uptime and response expected of a mission-critical compute campus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If it has a gas or steam turbine control system, a switchgear lineup, a plant electrical distribution network, a SCADA/DCS point, a control loop, or a supporting utility/process system (water, wastewater, fuel gas, HVAC, cooling) that must run reliably, this team designs it, specifies it, commissions it, and keeps it running. As a Manager, you will lead a team of engineers in a high-reliability, fast-paced environment. This is a hands-on technical leadership role — you will review P&amp;amp;IDs, challenge control philosophies, dive into DCS/PLC architecture, electrical protection schemes, and commissioning details, not just manage a roadmap. You will scale both the team and the systems as generation capacity and AI compute load grow.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own automation, controls, and electrical scope for power generation assets (gas turbine simple cycle, combined cycle, and steam turbine systems) and plant electrical systems, including DCS/SCADA architecture, PLC systems, turbine control interfaces, switchgear, protection and metering, plant distribution, instrumentation, and control networks — from control philosophy through commissioning and reliability, in compliance with NFPA 70/70B/70E, NESC, and IEEE standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead controls scope for mechanical and electrical balance-of-plant and supporting utilities, including fuel gas, HVAC, fire protection, compressed air, cooling water, raw water intake, demineralization, wastewater treatment, and industrial gas systems that keep the plant and downstream compute campus online.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, mentor, and manage a team of automation and controls engineers and technicians; scale the team with power generation capacity growth and AI supercomputer demand.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and approve control philosophy documents, I/O lists, control narratives, single-line diagrams, electrical/pneumatic schematics, cause-and-effect diagrams, and control panel designs; drive standardized DCS/PLC/SCADA architecture, cybersecurity posture, documentation, and engineering practices across the Southaven facilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with internal engineering, construction, OEMs (turbine, HRSG, BOP, and electrical equipment vendors), and contractors; develop SOWs, negotiate, and manage contractor work to keep controls and electrical scope integrated and on schedule.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own field commissioning for automation, controls, and electrical systems (loop checks, functional testing, protection testing, start-up, and hand-off) and drive root-cause investigations and reliability improvements on operating assets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Electrical Engineering, Controls Engineering, Automation Engineering, or related engineering field.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in automation and controls engineering, with direct experience on industrial power generation projects (gas turbine, combined cycle, or steam systems preferred) or large-scale critical power infrastructure.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience directly managing or leading a team of engineers (and preferably technicians).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCES:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with DCS, PLC, HMI, and SCADA platforms used in power generation or heavy industry (e.g., Emerson, ABB, Siemens, Allen-Bradley, SEL, Ignition), including IEC 61131 programming, industrial networking (IT/OT), and protocols such as Modbus and DNP3.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with gas turbine or combined-cycle plant controls (turbine control systems, HRSG controls, plant-wide DCS integration, and BOP), plus water treatment, wastewater, fuel gas, or process cooling systems supporting generation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of utility-scale and low-voltage electrical power systems, switchgear, protection, metering, and their interface with automation and controls.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or reviewing industrial control panels and electrical schematics (NFPA 79 / UL 508A; EPLAN, AutoCAD Electrical, or similar) across the full project lifecycle: design, procurement, construction support, commissioning, and operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing EPC and OEM interfaces on multi-discipline power or capital projects, and scaling a controls engineering function in a fast-growing organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PE license in Electrical or Controls Engineering (or willingness to pursue); familiarity with ICS cybersecurity frameworks (e.g., NERC CIP); experience supporting high-availability generation for critical or data center loads.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills with the ability to remain deeply technical while mentoring engineers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to perform hands-on work in all environments (heat, cold, rain), in tight quarters or at heights, while remaining focused in hazardous environments and wearing appropriate PPE; ability to lift up to 25 lbs unassisted.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work extended hours and weekends as needed, and to provide 24/7 on-call support for emergencies, to support power generation and critical compute operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work on-site at the Southaven power generation facility, with potential travel to other SpaceXSI sites.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Facilities Operations Manager at SpaceXSI Memphis, you will own the reliability, performance, and continuous improvement of critical data center infrastructure, including power, cooling, and environmental systems. You will lead and develop a team of Facilities Operations Supervisors and Technicians, driving hands-on technical excellence, strategic operational planning, process optimization, vendor management, and cross-functional collaboration. This role emphasizes building a high-performance, team-first culture while ensuring maximum uptime, safety, and efficiency across the site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and develop a team of Facilities Operations Supervisors and Technicians, fostering a culture of excellence, accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the overall maintenance, monitoring, troubleshooting, and performance of data center infrastructure, including HVAC, power distribution, UPS, generators, and environmental systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement, and continuously optimize preventive and predictive maintenance programs, equipment calibration strategies, and system performance KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, refine, and enforce standard operating procedures (SOPs), emergency response plans, and change management processes to drive operational consistency and excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure full compliance with safety regulations, industry standards, and internal policies; champion a strong safety culture across the facilities team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering, procurement, construction, and operations teams to streamline equipment intake, installation, commissioning, and lifecycle management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee inventory, asset management, and spare parts strategy using internal applications, ensuring accurate tracking, forecasting, and cost control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage critical equipment maintenance, repairs, and capital projects, ensuring timely resolution, rigorous documentation, and root-cause analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional initiatives to enhance operational efficiency, reduce downtime, and improve energy and resource utilization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own vendor relationships, service contracts, and performance management for critical facilities support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide 24/7 on-call leadership and drive rapid, effective response to critical facilities incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage operational budgets, forecasts, and resource planning for the facilities team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical, Electrical, or a related engineering field (relevant experience may substitute for degree).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience managing critical facilities systems, including power, cooling, and environmental controls in data center or mission-critical environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of people leadership experience in critical facilities or technical operations environments, including direct management of supervisors or technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of electrical, mechanical, and HVAC systems in data centers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of leading facilities infrastructure projects from planning through execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with building management systems (BMS), environmental monitoring tools, and computerized maintenance management systems (CMMS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong prioritization, time management, and decision-making skills under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-stakes environment while maintaining rigorous attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must pass pre-employment and annual post-employment background checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physical Requirements:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 35 lbs. unassisted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working at heights up to 50 feet with appropriate safety gear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in environments with exposure to noise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physical dexterity to perform job functions in confined spaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Availability to work evenings and weekends based on site operational needs; flexibility is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver’s license.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience programming or deeply configuring PLC-based control systems and advanced Building Management Systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project Management Professional (PMP) certification or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EPA Universal Refrigerant Certification (EPA 608 Technician).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing operational budgets and capital expenditure projects in a data center environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience scaling facilities operations in a high-growth technology or mission-critical setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MANAGER, FIBER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Manager, Fiber at SpaceXSI&#39;s Memphis data center, you will lead and oversee all fiber optic infrastructure activities, driving the successful execution of large-scale installations, maintenance, and optimization projects. You’ll combine hands-on technical expertise with strong leadership to manage teams of technicians, ensure the highest standards of safety and quality, and maintain the ultra-reliable high-speed connectivity that powers SpaceXSI&#39;s AI training and operations. Working closely with Foremen, Project Managers, and Superintendents, you’ll play a critical role in building and sustaining the robust network backbone essential to accelerating human scientific discovery through AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and supervise a team of Lead Fiber Technicians and Fiber Technicians in all datacenter fiber optic installation, maintenance, and repair activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee all phases of fiber optic projects from planning and execution to testing, handover, and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a safe, productive, high-quality, and compliant work environment for the entire fiber team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement sensor indicators, inspection protocols, and preventive maintenance routines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct complex troubleshooting, repair, splicing, and installation of fiber optics systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the inspection, replacement, and optimization of fiber optic cables and infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor signal strength, system performance, and resolve fiber optic problem areas proactively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate system records, documentation, as-built drawings, and design updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Project Managers, Superintendents, and other trades to coordinate cross-functional work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical guidance, training, performance feedback, and quality assurance across all fiber-related work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of direct data center experience installing, certifying, and maintaining optical fiber in large-scale Tier 3 or 4 facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience leading or supervising fiber optic teams in a commercial or data center environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification in fiber optics and/or cable installation (FOA, BICSI, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced expertise in fiber splicing, OTDR testing, and certification procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership and people-management experience in fast-paced construction or data center environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep technical knowledge of hyperscale data center networking, structured cabling, and fiber infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in AI/HPC data centers or other mission-critical facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with computers, fiber management software, and electronic testing systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving, communication, and organizational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in tight quarters with necessary physical dexterity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 35lbs, unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working at elevated heights (up to 50 feet) with appropriate safety gear&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in environments with high noise levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available to work evenings and weekends as needed; schedule flexibility is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Materials Management organization is a crucial part of data center operations, managing all critical materials to build and operate the world’s largest supercomputer clusters. Our goal is to become a leader in inventory performance with high accuracy and efficiency. The Manager will be responsible for managing day-to-day activities and exceeding customer expectations by leading continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform administrative duties, including but not limited to reviewing timecard compliance, scheduling, periodic reviews, supply ordering, one-on-one mentoring and training of direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and maintain operational targets and objectives for fulfillment, distribution, and storage centers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategy – Understand the processes, procedures, and needs of the business to develop strategy, business metrics, and goals to guide the organization in the direction needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership – Manage a multi-level deep organization, consisting of both hourly and salary individuals across 4 shift patterns that support 24/7 operations; assess employee performance, provide positive/constructive feedback, facilitate conflict resolution, and address repeat issues with corrective actions, performance improvement plans, or through disciplinary means.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Role Model – Lead by setting an example, taking feedback from all levels of the organization, and motivating your organization to achieve the highest level of results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safety – Monitor and improve operations, ensuring a safe work environment – with the goal of zero OSHA recordables annually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality – Ensure business practices not only guarantee the storing of product in a quality manner, but also meet those needs outlined in AS9100 and customer flow-down requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inventory Management – Manage the incoming receipt, acceptance, storage, and issuance of a wide variety of parts and hardware into inventory locations around campus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Service – Manage operations that provide industry leading levels of customer service in all operations: recognizing the needs of the business and adapting to support our mission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cost – Lead cost saving opportunities, identifying internal/external cost reductions and optimization opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inventory Accuracy – Maintain process control and routine counting required to meet both our internal and external audit requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process Improvement – Drive the projects and changes needed to ensure the distribution center can maintain rates year-over-year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shelf Life - Monitor shelf-life storage and maintain proper rotation of stock, FIFO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Environmental Controls – Ensure the appropriate environmental controls are in place, depending on the material requirements of the items being stored in the distribution center.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Storage – Manage and control the storage of non-SpaceX part numbers that need to be maintained for the business; this is a mixture of both internal and external storage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentorship – Actively monitor and grow the workforce, ensuring team members are challenged and performing at the expected standards; work to develop ways and methods to motivate team members to go above and beyond the status quo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptability – As SpaceX continues to innovate and pave the way for future development, this manager needs to be able to adapt his/her business to the ever-changing needs of the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree and 3+ years of experience working in one or more of the following: or bachelor’s degree and 5+ years of experience working in one or more of the following: or 9+ years of experience working in one or more of the following:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Material or production planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Purchasing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operations or supply chain management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Material cost control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master production scheduling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and self-driven, capable of working independently with little direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;APICS certification – CPIM or CSCP desired.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and team-building skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced /cross-functional environment while maintaining on-time project completion, deal with a wide variety of challenges, and work with a diverse array of contacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capable of adapting to abrupt changes in strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within an aerospace, aviation, or automotive manufacturing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience with capital planning and management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate innovative and futuristic thinking to drive continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computer Skills - Microsoft applications including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Visio, and Project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifting up to 50 lbs, standing, climbing, bending, grasping, sitting, pulling, pushing, stooping, stretching, and carrying are generally required to perform the functions of this position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work all shifts, extended hours and/or weekends as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to provide 24x7 on-call support in emergency situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is based in Memphis, TN and requires being onsite - remote work not considered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position may require domestic travel up to 20% as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MANAGER, OPERATION &amp;amp; MAINTENANCE (POWER PLANT)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Manager of Operation &amp;amp; Maintenance to lead the people who keep SpaceXSI’s on-site power plant running. You will oversee supervisors, leads, and technicians supporting operations and maintenance of gas turbine generation, balance-of-plant, process and fluid systems, and plant electrical systems. This plant supplies power for high-density AI supercomputing facilities in the Memphis and Southaven area, and it has to stay online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on leadership role. You will set the operating and maintenance standard, run the organization through trips, outages, and day-to-day work, and build supervisors and technicians who can execute safely without waiting on you for every decision. You will work with engineering, construction, operations leadership, OEMs, and contractors as the plant grows. This is a full-time, onsite role based in the Memphis region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own operation and maintenance of the power plant, including gas turbines and generators, balance-of-plant, fuel gas and process/fluid systems, water, compressed/instrument air, plant HVAC and cooling, and electrical systems through, including protection, e-houses, blackstart, and switching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead supervisors, leads, and technicians across plant, process, and electrical crafts as one O&amp;amp;M organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set daily and weekly priorities so planned maintenance, emergent work, alarms, trips, and outages are balanced without losing generation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the maintenance program: work planning, scheduling, procedures, CMMS discipline, spare parts readiness, and as-found/as-left documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct start-up, shutdown, switching, isolation, LOTO, and restoration so mechanical, process, and electrical work is coordinated and safe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce SpaceXSI safety standards, including LOTO, NFPA 70E / arc-flash, confined space, and hot work. Stop work when conditions are unsafe and hold the organization to that standard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead outage planning and execution with engineering, OEMs, and contractors, and support commissioning and turnover of new generation and BOP systems into operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own O&amp;amp;M vendor and contractor performance, cost, and schedule. Work with buyers and accounts payable so accounts and contracts stay in order&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive reliability: bad-actor elimination, root-cause investigations, and standards that raise uptime as capacity grows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and develop supervisors and leads. Set expectations, manage performance, and scale the team with the plant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate plant status, risks, team performance, and resource needs to site leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in a power plant or other high-reliability industrial operations and maintenance setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years directly managing supervisors, leads, or a multi-discipline technician organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a technical, engineering, or related field, or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating or maintaining gas turbine generation and balance-of-plant, including fuel gas, water, compressed air, and plant electrical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a mixed-discipline O&amp;amp;M team (plant, process, and electrical) in a generating station or similar facility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of P&amp;amp;IDs, single-line diagrams, electrical schematics, switching, LOTO, and NFPA 70E / arc-flash practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running a CMMS-based maintenance program, including planning, scheduling, and outage execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing O&amp;amp;M budgets, OEM service agreements, and third-party contractors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of reliability improvement, root-cause investigations, and high-uptime operation of mission-critical plant equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop supervisors and leads while staying close enough to the work to catch problems early&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication with technicians, engineers, contractors, and site leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to be in the plant and to perform hands-on work in all environments (heat, cold, rain), in tight quarters or at heights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work extended hours, nights, weekends, and on-call coverage to support plant operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remain focused while working in hazardous environments, while wearing appropriate PPE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to lift up to 25 lbs unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifting, standing, climbing, bending, grasping, sitting, pulling, pushing, stooping, stretching, and carrying are generally required to perform the functions of this position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work on-site at the power generation facility, with potential travel to other SpaceXSI sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceXSI operates multi-campus, hyperscale GPU infrastructure where cluster availability directly determines training throughput, customer handover commitments, and capital efficiency of the fleet. The Manager of Supercomputer Site Reliability Engineering will be responsible for both compute and infrastructure performance, and will be responsible for significantly increasing the SRE team size. On the compute side, focus will be put on continuous site monitoring, cross-discipline incident command, deep hardware root-cause analysis (RCA), and emphasis on software systems that orchestrate repair velocity. Additional focus will be on physical infrastructure reliability as well. Understanding system margins and resiliency will be key.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Site Reliability engineering manager owns &amp;gt;99% compute uptime outcome, drives unplanned facilities compute losses to 0, ensures efficient allocation of &amp;gt; 3GW site power, upgrade robust fault-free megapack failover systems capable of supporting all halls for &amp;gt;4 hours (160 MWhr per hall), drives robust hardware inventory systems and repair velocity to eliminate hardware chokepoints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the senior operational authority for the SRE organization and represent production reliability concerns in engineering and leadership discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead integrated Supercompute systems engineering reliability team responsible for reactive and increasingly proactive cluster and facilities health and reliance initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build out the site reliability engineering sub-teams: compute hardware failure analysis, software tools, cluster monitoring, and integrated site reliability engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive operational superiority&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define SRE organizational structure and develop culture of 24/7 operational excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physics limit anomaly response times and robust proactive health processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define on-call responsibilities, incident management protocols, leadership structure, and communication discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop training schemes for tough, competent, and disciplined monitoring and response teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear operational interfaces with Datacenter Operations, engineering teams, vendors, and other service owners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own vendor oversight and accountability mechanisms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive mean time to repair toward physics limits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and continuously improve operational procedures and analysis documentation mechanisms with strong emphasis on intelligent automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead robustification of documentation workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure efficient signal to noise in execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define operational targets, health indicators, alerting standards, and incident severity definitions that facilitate measurable team performance insights and accountability mechanisms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cultivate engineering excellence&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive high technical standard for hardware root cause analysis and remediation teams ensuring industry-leading hardware failure diagnostic expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate with platform engineering teams to develop sophisticated hardware and system understanding to drive high operational reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive repeat hardware issues to a minimum and lead automation efforts to eliminate manual overhead for unavoidable remediation needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree and 3+ years of experience working in a large scale operations with 2+ years leading people leaders of technical teams or 10+ years of experience working in a large scale operations with 5+ years leading people leaders of technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead large, multi-site, 24/7 operations organizations in fast-paced, high-responsibility settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in server hardware, cluster reliability, and data center technologies, from deployment through lifecycle management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting compute-heavy environments like AI, machine learning, or high-performance computing at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of owning uptime, Service Level Agreements, or reliability metrics for large compute clusters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading site reliability engineering or equivalent reliability-focused teams, including root cause analysis and procedure ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to diverse audiences, from technicians to executive and tenant partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of partnering with vendors at scale, driving mean time to repair down, and scaling operations across multiple sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with tooling and automation (e.g., Jira, Python, Bash) used to monitor cluster health and improve team efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiasm for SpaceXAI&#39;s mission to accelerate human discovery and unravel the universe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a dynamic, mission-focused environment with on-call ownership of cluster-impacting events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel frequently to data center locations to support operations across sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physical capability to handle data center tasks, including lifting up to 50 lbs unassisted, standing for long periods, and occasional ladder use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to work extended hours and/or weekends as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MATERIAL HANDLER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Material Handler is a support role for our large-scale data center construction project in Southaven, Mississippi. You will ensure construction, engineering, and trades teams have the materials they need every day. This position involves working directly in the field with planners, superintendents, technicians, and contractors to receive, stage, and deliver materials arriving at the site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-streamdown=&quot;unordered-list&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Interface with construction, engineering, and trades teams to identify and eliminate material bottlenecks in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Maintain clean, organized, and safe delivery and staging areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Receive, pick up, and deliver materials to multiple work areas across the data center campus and surrounding sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Stage and transport materials for daily work packages and project milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Operate material handling equipment (forklifts, pallet jacks, telehandlers, etc.) and maintain required operator qualifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Build and maintain staging/delivery locations as needed, including assembling shelving, posting signage, reorganizing inventory, relocating materials, and properly disposing of trash, packaging, and scrap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Expedite critical materials to meet construction schedules and completion dates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Use inventory and scheduling systems to manage, prioritize, and fulfill material requests from work packages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-streamdown=&quot;list-item&quot;&gt;Track and manage incoming deliveries and outgoing materials to ensure on-time availability at the point of use&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
