&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced Mechanical Commissioning Lead to lead the buildout, startup, and handover of mechanical systems for SpaceXSI&#39;s high-performance data centers. In this senior hands-on leadership role, you will direct commissioning, testing, troubleshooting, and turnover of critical cooling, air handling, and fluid distribution systems that support next-generation AI supercomputing infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead a team of commissioning technicians while working closely with construction, engineering, operations, EPC contractors, and OEM vendors to deliver safe, reliable, and high-quality mechanical systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and execute all mechanical commissioning activities for HVAC systems, chillers, cooling towers, CRAC/CRAH units, pumps, heat exchangers, piping systems, hydronic loops, and associated controls in hyperscale data center environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct functional performance testing, airflow/water flow verification, system balancing, integrated system testing, and system turnover to operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee troubleshooting and resolution of complex mechanical, controls, and process issues during pre-commissioning, commissioning, and startup phases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, review, and approve detailed commissioning test procedures, scripts, checklists, and documentation in alignment with project specifications, industry standards, and SpaceXSI requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead coordination with EPC contractors, OEM vendors, design engineers, and SpaceXSI stakeholders for system energization, startup sequences, and integrated system validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor, supervise, and provide technical direction to Mechanical Commissioning Technicians and other field personnel; conduct performance feedback and support their development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion safety by enforcing strict adherence to LOTO, NFPA, OSHA, and SpaceXSI safety protocols; lead daily safety briefings and job hazard analyses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain comprehensive as-built documentation, test records, issue logs, and final commissioning reports; present readiness reports to senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and deliver training programs for operations and maintenance teams on commissioned systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in constructability reviews, design feedback sessions, and lessons-learned meetings to continuously improve installation quality and future project execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage commissioning schedules, resources, and punch-list resolution to meet aggressive project timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of progressive hands-on mechanical commissioning experience in data centers, power plants, semiconductor facilities, or other industrial environments, with 3+ years in a lead or supervisory capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current OSHA 30 certification or equivalent certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in data center cooling systems including large-scale chillers, cooling towers, CRAC/CRAH units, precision air handling, chilled water plants, and high-density liquid cooling technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of commissioning test equipment (manometers, anemometers, ultrasonic flow meters, pressure/temperature calibrators, power analyzers, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough familiarity with relevant codes and standards (ASHRAE, SMACNA, NFPA, ASME, IMC, LEED, Uptime Institute)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to read, interpret, and redline mechanical drawings, P&amp;amp;IDs, control schematics, and sequence of operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership experience coordinating multi-discipline teams and managing contractors/vendors in fast-paced construction environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong safety leadership track record&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior leadership on multiple hyperscale data center or mission-critical commissioning projects (100+ MW scale preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NEBB, AABC, or equivalent Certification in Testing, Adjusting, and Balancing (TAB)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with BMS/BAS controls troubleshooting and integration (BACnet, Modbus, LON, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of refrigerant systems, direct liquid cooling, and advanced heat rejection technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with commissioning management platforms (CxPro, Procore, PlanGrid, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical degree or trade school certification in Mechanical Engineering Technology, HVAC, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing Integrated Systems Testing (IST) and Owner’s Project Requirements (OPR) verification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
