&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly skilled Mechanical Commissioning Technician to support the buildout and startup of SpaceXAI&#39;s high-performance data centers. In this critical hands-on role, you will perform commissioning, testing, and troubleshooting of mechanical systems that cool and support our next-generation AI supercomputing infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with construction, engineering, and operations teams to ensure safe, reliable, and high-quality mechanical systems from initial installation through full system turnover. This is a full-time, onsite role with significant travel to SpaceXAI data center sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute mechanical commissioning activities for chilled water, condenser water, cooling towers, pumps, heat exchangers, air handlers, computer-room cooling, liquid-cooling equipment, and associated controls in data center environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform flush, fill, leak, and pressure tests; verify valve lineup, flow, temperature, and pressure against design and sequence of operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete point-to-point checks with controls technicians and confirm sensors, actuators, interlocks, and alarms respond correctly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and resolve mechanical issues during pre-commissioning, commissioning, and startup phases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute detailed commissioning test procedures, scripts, and documentation in accordance with project specifications and industry standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with EPC contractors, OEM vendors, and SpaceXAI engineers to coordinate startup sequences and integrated system testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Walk systems against drawings, mark redlines, write punch-list items, and drive closeout until deficiencies are cleared.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure strict adherence to safety protocols, LOTO procedures, and quality standards during all commissioning activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate as-built documentation, test records, and commissioning reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support training of operations and maintenance teams on commissioned mechanical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in constructability reviews and provide field feedback to improve design and installation quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of hands-on mechanical, HVAC, pipefitting, or commissioning experience in data centers, power plants, or large industrial facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of chilled-water plants, pumping systems, heat transfer equipment, and related mechanical distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with commissioning and field test equipment (pressure gauges, flow meters, temperature instruments, leak-detection tools, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret piping and instrumentation diagrams, mechanical drawings, and equipment submittals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong safety mindset with current OSHA 10/30 or equivalent training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work extended hours, nights, and weekends during critical commissioning windows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
