&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a hands-on, safety-focused Megapack Field Technician to support the operation, maintenance, and expansion of our Megapack energy storage fleet powering SpaceXSI&#39;s AI infrastructure in Memphis. Working directly with the Energy Storage Asset Manager, you will own the low-voltage side of the fleet, support daily medium-voltage switching operations, and help manage construction and commissioning across multiple sites for one of the largest and most critical battery deployments powering AI training.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the low-voltage (LV) side of the Megapack fleet, including AC and DC LV systems, 480V auxiliary power, breakers, and LV terminations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform Megapack enable/disable, isolation, and return-to-service procedures in support of maintenance, switching, and construction activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot Megapack-side faults and alarms in the field, gather logs, data, and photos, and drive issues to resolution with OEM field service and support engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an onsite point of contact for Tesla Field Service technicians, coordinating access, isolations, and work scope to remove blockers and ensure high-quality, timely completion of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support execution of the daily medium-voltage (MV) switching plan, including de-energizing and re-energizing Megapack strings in coordination with MV electricians, testing contractors, and site operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform and verify lockout/tagout (LOTO) and maintain switching and isolation records in accordance with site safety procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide day-to-day oversight of electrical and civil contractors, verifying work against drawings, specifications, and schedule&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform quality checks on LV and MV terminations, installations, and repairs, and document findings for correction and closeout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate installation and commissioning activities for new Megapack deployments and their integration with SpaceXSI facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, track, and close out punch lists, performing field verification before items are closed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use drawings, single-line diagrams, and project management platforms (e.g., Procore) to track RFIs, submittals, and site issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support transformer issue intake and documentation, and assist with dehumidification and environmental controls during outages and construction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct routine site walks and inspections to identify safety, reliability, and serviceability issues before they impact operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate records of field work, switching activity, service events, and equipment status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure full compliance with all safety protocols, NFPA 70E requirements, manufacturer guidelines, and local regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide on-call support for urgent operational and maintenance issues as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of field service, commissioning, or maintenance experience on utility-scale battery energy storage systems (BESS) or power infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with low-voltage AC/DC electrical systems, breakers, and terminations, including safe isolation and verification of energy states&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of NFPA 70E, arc flash safety, and lockout/tagout procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and work from electrical drawings, single-line diagrams, and equipment documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and organizational skills with the ability to coordinate multiple contractors and vendors in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working onsite in an industrial/data center and active construction environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utility-scale BESS field service experience (Megapack preferred), including Megapack 2 / 2XL installation, commissioning, service, and troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with OEM service and diagnostic tools, firmware updates, and site controller workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting medium-voltage switching operations, string energization, or utility/data center switching programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Construction management or field engineering experience, including contractor oversight, QA/QC, punch lists, and Procore or similar platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with pad-mount transformers, medium-voltage cable and terminations, and fire protection standards for energy storage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in 24/7 operational environments with on-call responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position is subject to pre-employment and annual post-employment background checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in an environment requiring exposure to noise, outdoor weather, and industrial conditions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available to work evenings, weekends, and provide on-call support as needed for urgent operational issues and planned outages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift 50+ pounds, climb, and work at heights and in confined spaces as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver&#39;s license and ability to travel between Memphis-area sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a full-time, onsite role based in Memphis, Tennessee, with regular travel between Memphis-area sites&lt;/li&gt;
