&lt;p&gt;Join the High Power Engineering team supporting SpaceXSI to design, build, operate, and maintain electrical infrastructure for AI training campuses. As a Ops/Build Engineer on the Transmission &amp;amp; Distribution team, you will work with a small on-site team to scale high-capacity power systems on a schedule set by compute demand. The position is based in Memphis, TN, with potential travel to other sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take high- and medium-voltage assets from steel in the ground to carrying load, then own their reliability in operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the substation and transmission energization plan: pre-energization checks, phasing verification, synchronizing checks, and staged load ramp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct NETA acceptance testing on breakers, transformers, GIS, instrument transformers, arresters, and cable systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute relay end-to-end testing, transfer trip verification, and point-to-point SCADA and telemetry checkout with the site and the utility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate outages and switching with the utility; write and own clearance and switching procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute the electrical safety program in the field: arc-flash labeling currency, energized work permitting, and switching authorization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;After energization, own transformer oil program, breaker maintenance intervals, battery and charger program, SF6 monitoring, and fault investigation using relay event records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with construction, vendors, and technicians; drive rapid, continuous improvements at the Memphis campus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with NFPA 70, 70B, 70E, NESC, and IEEE standards, prioritizing safety and engineering excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in electrical engineering, computer engineering, physics, or another engineering discipline, or 8+ years of substation field experience in lieu of a degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in substation commissioning, testing, build, or utility operations on high-power, high-voltage systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience energizing high-voltage equipment and directing switching on live systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with relay test sets such as Doble F6150 or Omicron CMC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NETA Level III or IV certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SEL relay families.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NERC PRC compliance testing and evidence experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to quickly troubleshoot issues and support technicians hands-on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead teams, work independently, and thrive in dynamic, high-stress environments with tight deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
