&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Data Center Engineering team designs training and inference compute clusters from first principles, pushing thermal, electrical, and optical systems to the limit of physics. We operate as a highly cross-disciplinary team of mechanical, electrical, optical, and software engineers, all working to maximize the efficiency, reliability, and deployment speed of terrestrial computing to serve rapidly scaling demand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This team owns compute architecture, datacenter network design, rack builds, connectivity, in-house design of our own computers, and the manufacturing line that builds that compute. As an Optical Engineer, you will own the physical optical layer of that computer: fiber layout, link design, connector and polarity architecture, optics selection, and production of a plant that can be built, tested, and repaired at AI cluster scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end optical and fiber design for AI training and inference fabrics: fiber cabling, cassette/panel architecture, polarity, breakout, reach, and connector strategy (MPO-12/16, SN, MDC, LC, OSFP / QSFP-DD)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and verify link budgets for scale-out and scale-up interconnect (SMF/MMF, AOC/DAC, DR/FR/LR, InfiniBand and Ethernet), including loss, reflections, FEC, and realistic install margins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement factory tests for optical interconnects including insertion loss, return loss, and polarization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select and qualify optics, fiber, and connectivity (transceivers, patch, trunks, cassettes, harnesses); own vendor bring-up, failure analysis, and fleet reliability of the optical layer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy and verify end-to-end optical interconnect into the manufacturing line&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead commissioning and debug: inspect/clean, power meter, OTDR, BER/FEC stats, and volume failure modes (dirty connectors, wrong polarity, wrong map, damaged end-face)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve connectivity toward the next speed and density (800G / 1.6T, CPO/NPO awareness, tighter reaches, higher fiber count per rack)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Work with mechanical and network teams to design structured cabling and raceways with the rack and facilities teams: tray fill, bend radius, pre-term vs field-term, labeling, and a plant that can be built and repaired at hall scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in electrical engineering, optical engineering, physics, or a related engineering discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of professional experience in fiber layout, optical link design, and/or datacenter/HPC optical engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of fiber or optical design that was installed and turned up in a datacenter, HPC, or AI-compute environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working command of single-mode vs multimode, MPO polarity, insertion/return loss, and 100G+ transceiver classes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on optical test: inspect/clean, power meter, OTDR or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fiber interconnect ownership for AI / high-compute clusters (GPU scale-out fabric, InfiniBand NDR/XDR, RoCE Ethernet 400/800G)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-density pre-terminated trunk/cassette design and rack-to-spine optical mapping at hall scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optics vendor qualification at volume (OSFP, 800G DR8/2xFR4, AOCs, and the failure modes that show up in a real fleet)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing optical harnesses or cassettes for a manufacturing line, including test coverage and yield&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DWDM / campus DCI for cluster-to-cluster or building-to-building connectivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CPO/NPO, linear-drive optics, and next-gen packaging as it hits the rack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time at a high-velocity AI cloud, GPU cloud, or custom-compute hardware team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to work extended hours and weekends as needed to support design releases, line bring-up, and cluster deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to travel to manufacturing and datacenter sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in active datacenter and factory environments, including fiber inspection, cleaning, and live debug&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OSP ENGINEER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will support the design, documentation, and coordination of outside plant (OSP) fiber optic infrastructure. Focuses on producing accurate construction drawings, route maps, and as-built records using AutoCAD and GIS tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and revise OSP fiber design drawings, conduit layouts, splice diagrams, and permitting packages in AutoCAD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain GIS-based route maps, asset inventories, and spatial data for fiber pathways, vaults, and handholes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with field surveys, redline markups, and conversion of field data into final drawings and GIS layers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support BOM development, quantity take-offs, and basic loss-budget calculations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with senior engineers, construction teams, and utilities on design changes and as-built updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure drawings and GIS data comply with company standards, TIA/BICSI guidelines, and local permitting requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate’s degree in engineering, geospatial technology, or scientific discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GIS software (ArcGIS, QGIS, or equivalent) for mapping and spatial analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of AutoCAD (preferably Civil 3D or similar) for utility/telecom drawings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of fiber optic OSP concepts (conduit systems, aerial/buried placement, splicing, and terminations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and ability to produce clear, accurate technical drawings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior internship or project experience in telecom, utility, or civil infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with fiber strand counts, duct banks, and standard OSP construction practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Google Earth, KML/KMZ files, or CAD-to-GIS data exchange&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to perform occasional field work and site visits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;SpaceXSI is looking for an exceptional network engineer with experience in mission-critical or large-scale production environments to support our supercomputer infrastructure. As a member of the Physical Infrastructure Networking team, you will provide operational and designs services for physical infrastructure networks. The ideal candidate thrives in intense, high flux environments, brings a strong sense of urgency balanced with operational excellence, communicates effectively, and demonstrates high levels of technical acumen.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement highly available networks, carefully balancing various routing and redundancy technologies depending on unique requirements between production and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain mission data center and site networks in accordance with company network standards. Collaborating with adjacent infrastructure and enterprise teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, procure, and deploy network hardware including switches, firewalls, multiplexing and SDWAN appliances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to ever maturing network automation tooling; implementing configuration analysis, linting, and scalability into the deployment framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and coordinate network outage windows with stakeholders to perform software updates, hardware refreshes, and general network maintenance (sometimes on weekends and evenings).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and resolve network-related issues, publishing root cause analysis (RCA) documentation and hosting retrospective data reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide direct networking support during launch and test campaigns and be on-call or provide real-time support as networking responsible engineer during operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively tailors network monitoring to provide ever more valuable operational telemetry with emphasis on issue detection prior to operational impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously create and update network documentation, including architecture overviews, design drawings, and operational procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams to proactively identify and resolve potential technical issues with network designs, especially in regards to systemic, cascading failure modes, and superficial redundancy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform job walks with customers, vendors, and contractors to gather network requirements and create implementation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure networks are configured and maintained in compliance with industry and cybersecurity standards (e.g., ITAR, ISO, NIST), with particular attention to controls network segmentation and security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and validate resilient, scalable multi-site OT network topologies optimized for critical facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit, and enforce zero-trust firewalls to decouple facility infrastructure from the corporate DMZ.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author comprehensive system/network architecture drawings, IP/VLAN schemes, and data flow diagrams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support on-site system deployment, physical network cutovers, and new site commissioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in computer science, computer engineering, or other STEM discipline and 3+ years of professional network engineering experience;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OR 5+ years of professional network engineering experience in lieu of a degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of hands-on experience in Operational Technology (OT) networking, critical facility infrastructure, industrial automation, or controls engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive hands-on experience designing, deploying, supporting, and troubleshooting Layer 2 and Layer 3 networks in latency sensitive and/or industrial environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Functional experience with multiple network vendors either in production or lab environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GitOps and Infrastructure as Code Frameworks, both as user and contributor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the OSI model and network standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Cisco, Arista, and Juniper data center class switches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Wave Division Multiplexing (WDM) and fiber optics infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of common enterprise and media protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with switch port security features, network segmentation, QoS, multicast, and redundancy protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with network monitoring tools and layer 1 testing tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in scripting (Bash/PowerShell/Python) and automation frameworks (Terraform, Ansible, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Linux and Windows system administration experience professionally or from labs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry standard certifications such as CCNA or CCNP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting real-time systems, industrial control networks, or operational technology (OT) environments in aerospace, defense, energy, oil &amp;amp; gas, or similar high-reliability industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills with the ability to communicate with internal/external customers, vendors, and management in both formal and informal situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in tight quarters; physical dexterity is necessary to perform job functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Availability for extended hours and/or weekends as the schedule varies depending on site operational needs; flexibility is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to provide 24x7 on-call support in emergency situations and participate in an after-hours on-call rotation.&lt;/li&gt;
