&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the High Power Engineering team supporting SpaceXSI to design, build, operate, and maintain electrical infrastructure for AI training campuses. As a Power System Engineer on the Transmission &amp;amp; Distribution team, you will work with a small on-site team to scale high-capacity power systems on a schedule set by compute demand. The position is based in Memphis, TN, with potential travel to other sites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the single model of record for the Memphis campus: load flow, short circuit, coordination, arc flash, motor starting, harmonics, transient stability, and EMT studies for grid-forming inverter interaction with generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain sitewide power budgets, monitoring, and metering for mission-critical assets to optimize visibility and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform detailed analysis on electrical power systems: one-lines, three-lines, studies that justify relay settings, and as-built model updates after commissioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed interconnection studies, relay settings, arc-flash labels, and Battery Storage sizing from the same model. Do not allow shadow models in other pillars.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop standardized study cases for hall add, storage dispatch, islanding, and black start.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with NFPA 70, 70B, 70E, NESC, and IEEE standards, prioritizing safety and engineering excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in electrical engineering, computer engineering, physics, or another engineering discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in power systems design, analysis, and studies, with a focus on high-power, high-voltage systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with power systems analysis software and tools: ETAP, SKM, EasyPower, PowerWorld, Matlab, PSCAD, PSS/E, ASPEN, Simulink, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience performing load flow, short-circuit, arc-flash, coordination, and transient stability studies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with industrial power systems up to 345 kV, including switchgear, transformers, BESS, VFDs, motors, distribution systems, UPS/emergency backups, power generation, relaying, metering, protective devices, and networking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional Engineering license or intention to actively seek a PE license.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CAD software: Revit, AutoCAD, NX, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated initiative, creative problem-solving, and strong analytical/engineering fundamentals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform hands-on work in all environments (heat, cold, rain), in tight quarters or at heights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work extended hours and weekends as needed to support construction, energization, and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remain focused in hazardous environments while wearing appropriate PPE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lift up to 25 lbs. unassisted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide 24/7 on-call support for emergencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to work on-site in Memphis, TN. This is not a remote or hybrid role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel up to 25% for factory witness testing, vendor and OEM engagement, and supporting other sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver&#39;s license.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POWER SYSTEMS ENGINEER, DATA CENTER INFRASTRUCTURE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the facility operations team, you will design, build, and activate some of the world’s most technically advanced facilities and data centers. As an electrical engineer, you will design and build power systems that directly contribute to new infrastructure projects. You will be able to operate with autonomy to solve diverse and complex problems, excel at managing multiple projects simultaneously, and work in a dynamic, fast-paced environment. You will work with other MEP engineers, trade partners, and internal customers to support these goals and have the opportunity to drive real global impact, ultimately leading to making life multiplanetary.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in a team environment with other engineering disciplines to provide detailed electrical design and specification for the installation of the following equipment and systems: electrical power distribution systems, switch-gear and motor control centers, exterior and interior lighting, ground support system controls and ladder logic, uninterruptible power supply (UPS) units, standby and emergency generators, automatic transfer switches, power monitoring hardware and software, data/phone distribution and wiring, building and site grounding systems, and fire&amp;nbsp;alarm systems and lightning protection systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide electrical engineering support to facility technicians to troubleshoot existing electrical equipment and controllers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide engineering support for the design, operation, and troubleshooting of all the facility&#39;s electrical components and systems, including load flow analysis of electrical power distribution systems, electrical equipment evaluation, building and facility equipment grounding, and power monitoring hardware and software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that all equipment interfaces properly with other mechanical and electrical systems, including compatibility with facility power budgets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate all electrical installations and maintenance activities with local electrical utilities personnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all electrical designs and installations conform to applicable codes and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide code review and analysis utilizing NFPA 70E, NFPA 70 NEC, NFPA 497, NFPA 101, Vol 5 &amp;amp; 6 AFSPCMAN 91-710, and IBC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in electrical engineering or other engineering discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional experience working on electrical projects, power distribution systems, switchgear, UPS&#39;s, and/or generators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience in a similar role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional Engineering (PE) license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and understand power and control schematics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and understand highly technical equipment operation and maintenance (O&amp;amp;M) manuals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with variable frequency drives (VFDs) and industrial pumps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with controls in MODBUS communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with medium voltage distribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with control panel design and production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of power coordination and arc flash&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work on multiple tasks concurrently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of self-motivation, with the ability to work under minimal supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good organizational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize and schedule workload&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Process Technician is responsible for building, installing, operating, and troubleshooting fluid and process systems at SpaceXSI&#39;s power generation facility. This role focuses on plant fluid systems including fuel gas, ammonia, water, compressed and instrument air, and HVAC. Technicians play a key role in the design and commissioning process by providing feedback to engineers on how systems will be operated and maintained.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support fuel gas, ammonia, water/cooling water, compressed and instrument air, HVAC, and related balance-of-plant process systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read and interpret planning documents, P&amp;amp;IDs, schematics, data sheets/manuals, drawings, blueprints, and engineering sketches&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adjust, repair, or replace faulty components of process, utility, and plant fluid equipment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect and verify pressure transducers, thermocouples, and other sensors&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete necessary wiring of electrical support equipment for process and utility systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform high-pressure liquid and pneumatic testing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and repair high-urgency operational issues found during commissioning, start-up, outages, or normal plant operation of fluid systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow lockout/tagout, hot work, confined space, and other site safety procedures while working on live and isolated process systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with fluids, mechanical, and controls engineers to walk down systems, redline drawings, and improve operability and maintainability&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience using mechanical and/or electronics hand tools&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience with pipe fitting and fabrication&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of Microsoft Office (Excel, PowerPoint, Word, Outlook)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience maintaining and troubleshooting complex fluid and mechanical systems in a power plant, process plant, or similar industrial facility&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with fuel gas, ammonia, water treatment or cooling water, compressed/instrument air, HVAC, or hydraulic/pneumatic systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with orbital or structural welding&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with pneumatic/hydraulic system fabrication&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional experience with calibrated measuring instruments&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using heavy equipment, including but not limited to overhead cranes, forklifts, and manlifts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read P&amp;amp;IDs and support system commissioning and outage work&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to lift at least 25 lbs (unassisted)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to travel up to 25%. Position is based at a SpaceXSI power generation facility; work at other SpaceXSI sites for extended periods for similar work may be required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to climb ladders and work in confined spaces&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be available to work overtime, weekends, and rotating shifts as needed based on plant operational needs; flexibility required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in all environments (heat, cold, rain) while wearing appropriate PPE&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
