&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JD degree and bar admission or equivalent and in good standing to practice law in your relevant jurisdiction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of legal experience is preferred in areas covering AI, privacy, consumer protection, and content regulation law; we don’t expect every candidate to have experience in each field, but some combination thereof&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills and the ability to explain complex ideas in a succinct and impactful manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regulatory and in-house experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solution-oriented, customer service, and growth mindset - you welcome diverse perspectives and engage problems with curiosity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to integrate into cross-functional teams with a cooperative and participatory approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as an in-house adviser for consumer platforms in the social media sector, dealing with issues related to personalization and data protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is not a remote or hybrid position. The position will be based out of our Palo Alto office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
