&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Production Coordinator is a linchpin role within SpaceXSI&#39;S logistics organization supporting data center construction, commissioning, and ongoing campus operations. Production Coordinators work with logistics leadership, inventory, receiving, Site Operations, and construction teams to ensure the on-time delivery of components, kits, and assemblies for hyperscale AI training infrastructure. This position is based in Memphis, TN / Southaven, MS, with work across the Memphis / Southaven campus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create inventory requests based on work orders, kits, and replacement parts for data center build and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain material and production schedules through coordination of planning and shortage management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure parts and equipment are handled and protected properly and within SpaceXSI specifications, including high-value servers, networking gear, power and cooling components, and infrastructure materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with engineers, technicians, Site Operations, and construction on the release of work orders and material requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile work order bill of material quantities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain high integrity in company computer systems per procedures; assist with resolution of incorrect system data that drives inappropriate demand, schedules, or could result in general failure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify all material received for conformity with accompanying paperwork, checking for damage, correct part numbers, quantity, and revisions prior to release of work orders or kits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with internal customers for priority and schedule requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist materials management leadership and project teams with action item updates as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate part status and estimated completion dates to leadership upon request&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist logistics and operations teams in corrective actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support logistics process through innovative staging of workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform de-kitting operations and own the return-to-stock process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support productivity improvement across receiving, inventory, kitting, and material flow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ year(s) of supply chain, inventory, or manufacturing experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of MRP/ERP systems (SAP, Oracle, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate’s degree in a business or technology field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in data center, aerospace, automotive, semiconductor, or electronic manufacturing environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating forklifts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;APICS certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver’s license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work at elevated heights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in extreme outdoor environments — heat, cold, rain, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in an environment requiring exposure to fumes, odors, and noise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to operate machinery such as forklifts and loaders when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available for overtime and weekends as the schedule varies depending on site operational needs; flexibility required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to and available for travel (up to 20% of time)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work onsite in the Memphis, TN / Southaven, MS area&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PROGRAM MANAGER, DATA CENTER CONSTRUCTION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced&amp;nbsp;Program Manager, Data Center Construction to lead our growing portfolio of data center and infrastructure construction programs. In this leadership role, you will oversee multiple Construction Project Managers and ensure the successful delivery of complex, mission-critical facilities that support SpaceXSI&#39;s AI supercomputing goals. You will serve as a key bridge between field execution, engineering, and executive leadership, driving program-level strategy, risk management, and operational excellence in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic leadership and direct management to a team of Construction Project Managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee end-to-end execution of multiple large-scale construction programs, including pre-construction planning, site development, procurement, construction, commissioning, and handover for data centers and supporting infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align program deliverables with SpaceXSI&#39;s broader infrastructure roadmap, AI compute requirements, and aggressive timelines through close collaboration with engineering, design, commissioning, operations, and executive teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage program-level budgets, schedules, resources, and risks; develop and maintain master schedules, forecasts, and contingency plans to ensure on-time, on-budget delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a senior owner’s representative, managing relationships with general contractors, subcontractors, vendors, permitting authorities, and internal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive standardized processes, best practices, and performance metrics (KPIs, dashboards, reporting) across projects while identifying and implementing value engineering, cost-saving opportunities, and innovations in construction means and methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure rigorous safety, quality, and compliance standards, including adherence to relevant codes, environmental regulations, and SpaceXSI&#39;s high-reliability requirements for mission-critical facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and resolve cross-project issues, escalate appropriately, and lead recovery efforts when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support continuous improvement by mentoring teams, conducting lessons-learned reviews, and contributing to the evolution of SpaceXSI&#39;s construction program management framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt flexibly to evolving priorities in a dynamic, high-growth organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in construction management, civil/mechanical/electrical engineering, or scientific discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of progressive experience in construction project/program management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of direct people management experience leading teams of Project Managers, Superintendents, or similar roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in project/program management with a strong focus on data centers, hyperscale facilities, mission-critical infrastructure, or large industrial projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record delivering complex programs on aggressive schedules and within budget in fast-paced environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical knowledge across multiple disciplines (civil/site, structural, MEP, controls, commissioning) with the ability to interpret drawings, specifications, and technical requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent leadership, communication, and stakeholder management skills, with experience presenting to executive audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with construction management tools (e.g., Procore, Primavera P6, Bluebeam, MS Project) and data-driven decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data center or hyperscale construction (ground-up builds, MEP-intensive facilities, liquid cooling, power infrastructure)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional certifications such as PMP, CCM, PE, or LEED&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Memphis/Shelby County or similar regional permitting, codes, and construction practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in high-growth tech or industrial environments with a focus on speed, innovation, and operational readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build high-performing teams and implement program governance in matrixed organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subject to pre-employment and random drug/alcohol testing, background checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in active construction site environments (noise, outdoor exposure, ability to lift 25+ lbs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility for evenings/weekends as project needs dictate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel as needed and work flexible hours to support site operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a full-time, primarily onsite role based in the Memphis, TN area, with flexibility for travel to support additional project sites across the US&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We serve our community of users and customers by working tirelessly to preserve free expression and choice, create limitless interactivity, and maintain a safe digital marketplace. The Safety Integrity Program Manager, Harmful Activity will drive priorities, measures, and system health for harmful activity, owning program standards and execution across upstream systems and downstream operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an experienced program manager with a strong background in content integrity, abuse, or risk programs at scale. You are skilled at setting requirements for detection and automation, translating policy and legal constraints into practical workflows and controls, and driving cross-functional partners to improve coverage, precision, and enforcement quality. You thrive in fast-paced environments and excel at turning operational signals into lasting improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive priorities, measures, and system health for harmful activity, and continuously improve execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set requirements and success criteria for detection and automation, and drive Product, Engineering, and Operations to improve coverage, precision, and enforcement quality at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate legal, policy, and technical constraints into practical requirements, workflows, controls, and escalation paths for Product, Engineering, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps in the current framework and drive enhancements to policies, procedures, controls, and workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own escalations, quality assurance, and complex case patterns for residual volume, and use those signals to harden standards and automation over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align and drive Product, Engineering, Policy, Legal, and Operations partners to resolve dependencies, make decisions, and move critical work forward with clear accountable ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the documentation, guidance, and operating standards that embed consistent execution across the program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor relevant regulatory developments, assess impact on the program, and ensure requirements stay accurate and executable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report operational performance, risks, and improvement opportunities with clear recommendations for leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in content integrity, safety operations, abuse operations, or related program roles supporting enforcement or risk programs at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning or supporting program priorities, measures, and operational health for content or risk domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of harmful activity domains and how policy, legal, and technical constraints shape response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating policy or legal requirements into practical workflows, controls, and escalation paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with automated or model-driven enforcement systems, including detection, classifiers, or policy automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to drive cross-functional work with Product, Engineering, Policy, Legal, and Operations partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills with experience using operational data to identify gaps, prioritize interventions, and track outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication; able to brief leadership and document standards, decisions, and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
