&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a mid-to-senior Governance, Risk, and Compliance (GRC) professional focused on third-party risk management and customer trust. This role sits at the intersection of cybersecurity GRC, vendor management, and sales enablement: you will act as a security-minded presales engineer for the sales team, develop enough depth in the SpaceXSI technical environment to accurately complete customer vendor security questionnaires, join customer meetings as the security and compliance subject matter expert, and help operate third-party risk and vendor management processes. The ideal candidate brings a cybersecurity and GRC perspective — fluent in how AI LLMs, CI/CD pipelines, identity and access management, DevOps, DevSecOps, Kubernetes, and IT/AI governance actually work in production — and can translate that understanding into clear, credible answers for enterprise buyers without slowing deals or overstating our posture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role may also include additional tasks and responsibilities as needed to support the team and evolving business priorities.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the sales organization as a cybersecurity/GRC presales partner: attend customer and prospect meetings, present our security and compliance posture, and answer technical and control-related questions with accuracy and judgment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and continuously improve responses to customer vendor security questionnaires, RFPs, SIG/CAIQ-style assessments, and due-diligence requests; maintain a reusable knowledge base of control narratives grounded in how SpaceXSI actually operates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain working fluency across the SpaceXSI environment — AI/LLM systems and model governance, CI/CD pipelines, identity and access management, DevOps and DevSecOps practices, Kubernetes platforms, and governance of IT and AI environments — sufficient to answer customer questions and escalate appropriately to engineering when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering, Security, Legal, and Product to keep questionnaire content, Trust Center materials, and security collateral current as architecture, controls, and certifications evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer security requirements into actionable internal asks; help distinguish must-have contractual or control commitments from unreasonable or out-of-scope demands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to policies, standards, and procedures related to third-party risk, customer assurance, and vendor security due diligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with the broader GRC and security teams on overlapping frameworks and evidence (e.g., SOC 2, ISO 27001, ISO 42001, privacy commitments) so external answers remain consistent with our internal control environment and GRC tooling (e.g., Vanta).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify patterns in customer questionnaires and deal blockers; feed those insights back into product, engineering, and GRC roadmaps to reduce friction over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and present concise status updates on questionnaire volume, deal-impacting security asks, vendor risk posture, and emerging customer assurance themes to sales leadership and GRC stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion clear, honest customer communication — building trust by explaining what we do, how we govern AI and infrastructure, and where we are intentionally scoping risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in computer science, Information Security, Cybersecurity, or in an engineering/STEM field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in cybersecurity, GRC, third-party risk management, security assurance, or a closely related role with customer-facing or sales-adjacent responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience completing or owning customer vendor security questionnaires and participating in security due-diligence discussions with enterprise buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working technical fluency across several of the following: AI/LLM or ML platforms, CI/CD pipelines, identity and access management, DevOps/DevSecOps, Kubernetes, and cloud environments (AWS, GCP, or Azure) — enough to understand control implications and speak credibly with engineers and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of common security and compliance frameworks used in customer assurance (e.g., SOC 2, ISO 27001, NIST CSF) and how controls map to questionnaire language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain cybersecurity and GRC concepts to sales, customers, legal, and engineering audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of cybersecurity, GRC, third-party risk, or customer trust / security assurance experience (mid-to-senior scope).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a presales security, solutions engineering (security), customer trust, or sales-enablement GRC role at a technology, cloud, or AI company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on or deeply adjacent experience with vendor risk management programs — onboarding assessments, continuous monitoring, contract security exhibits, and residual-risk reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI governance topics relevant to customer diligence (e.g., model data handling, prompt/output controls, training-data boundaries, ISO 42001 / NIST AI RMF concepts, EU AI Act awareness).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience maintaining a Trust Center, security FAQ library, or questionnaire knowledge base; familiarity with GRC platforms such as Vanta, Drata, or similar is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read architecture diagrams, IAM models, and pipeline/Kubernetes high-level designs and turn them into accurate, non-jargon customer narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in fast-moving deal cycles while protecting accuracy — knowing when to say &quot;I&#39;ll confirm with engineering&quot; versus answering from established evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of data privacy frameworks (e.g., GDPR, CCPA) as they appear in enterprise security and vendor assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certifications such as CISSP, CISA, CISM, CRISC, CTPRP, CIPT, CIPP/US, or similar preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting public sector, financial services, or other highly regulated customer diligence processes is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;$100,000 - $228,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Base salary is just one part of our total rewards package at SpaceXSI, which also includes equity, comprehensive medical, vision, and dental coverage, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, short &amp;amp; long-term disability insurance, life insurance, and various other discounts and perks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a class=&quot;discussion-id-36164de2-197a-8070-84b2-001c900d71fe notion-link-token notion-focusable-token notion-enable-hover&quot; href=&quot;https://deccs.pmddtc.state.gov/deccs&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;link-annotation-unknown-block-id--1213793699&quot;&gt;here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SECURITY ENGINEER, KUBERNETES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We protect the platform that runs X and SpaceXSI. We don’t just report issues, we actively look for real risks and exploits in our Kubernetes environments and turn them into durable fixes and tooling. You will secure the platform behind X and SpaceXSI’s infrastructure, products, and workloads. If you know pod and platform security, think in attack paths, and want to build the defenses that make the platform safer at scale, we want to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value a understanding of how Kubernetes can actually be abused – not just how it is configured. We prioritize shipping practical controls and tooling over writing policy documents, applying least privilege and defense-in-depth at fleet scale, delivering clear findings and fixes that platform teams can act on, and conducting safe, constrained validation that does not put production at risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure the platform end to end: nodes, clusters, pods, roles, tokens, secrets, service-to-service communication, and the supply chain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find and remediate overprivileged permissions, dangerous pod and workload settings, and escalation paths in operators, admission, networking, identity, and monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess our own platform the way an adversary would, including container and pod breakout, privilege escalation, and movement across workloads, using safe and constrained validation, then fix what you find&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build security tooling and automation, including AI-assisted analysis, that catches risky configuration and overprivilege before or after it ships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen identity and secrets handling so workloads receive only the access they need&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve supply-chain security through secure base images, continuous scanning, and related controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review changes that affect RBAC, operators, ServiceAccounts, network policies, and anything running with elevated privileges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with platform and product teams as a security owner, taking problems from identification through rollout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to fleet-wide hardening, policy enforcement, and safer defaults&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years in platform security, Kubernetes security, or offensive security against production infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of pod and workload security: privileged containers, capabilities, host namespaces, host path mounts, service accounts, RBAC, admission control, and network isolation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of identity, secrets, workload identity, service-to-service trust, supply chain, runtime, and cloud access&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to think like an attacker, measure blast radius, and turn the path into a detection, control, or tool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with operators, custom resources, Helm, and GitOps workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to build or modify security tooling in Go, Python, or Rust when a control needs automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus:&amp;nbsp;Image scanning, SBOMs, secure base images, policy-as-code (Kyverno, OPA), multi-cluster environments, runtime detection, and security testing of customer-facing application&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing AI-driven security tools or integrating AI into security workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Kubernetes-based environments and securing cloud-native infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to drive technical decisions and influence security practices across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for challenging the status quo and building transformative security solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills, with experience working in dynamic, cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sense of humor and adaptability to thrive in a fast-paced, mission-driven environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open to working out of one of our offices: Palo Alto, Austin, DC, or New York&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$100,000 - $258,000 USD&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary is just one part of our total rewards package at SpaceXSI, which also includes equity, comprehensive medical, vision, and dental coverage, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, short &amp;amp; long-term disability insurance, life insurance, and various other discounts and perks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced BSA/AML Investigator to help detect, prevent, and report financial crimes. As part of the Legal &amp;amp; Compliance Team, you will help maintain an effective BSA/AML and Sanctions compliance program (“BSA/AML Program”) for X Money. You will support the 5 pillars of an effective program.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a remote or hybrid position. This role is based on-site at either our Palo Alto headquarters or New York City office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently investigate and resolve complex alerts and cases from transaction monitoring systems, including in-depth analysis of payment flows and user behaviors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare, review, and recommend filing of Suspicious Activity Reports (SARs), ensuring high-quality narratives and supporting documentation.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with KYC and onboarding matters as required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD) on high-risk users and transactions; perform periodic reviews of customer risk profiles and recommend adjustments to risk ratings.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in tuning and optimizing transaction monitoring rules and scenarios to reduce false positives while maintaining detection effectiveness.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and provide guidance to junior team members on investigation techniques and regulatory requirements.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal teams (e.g., Product, Risk, Legal) on compliance-related initiatives and new product launches.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain expertise in evolving BSA/AML/OFAC regulations, FinCEN guidance, and payment industry financial crime trends.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of hands-on experience in AML, ideally in fintech or banking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with financial crime risks specific to digital payments, money transmission, wallets, or peer-to-peer platforms is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience preparing and filing SARs, including high-quality, well-structured narratives — strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of BSA/AML laws and regulations, including the Bank Secrecy Act (BSA), USA PATRIOT Act, OFAC sanctions, and related requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven familiarity with local, regional, and international regulatory bodies (e.g., FinCEN, FATF, or equivalent), with practical experience navigating their guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to drive operational changes, manage competing priorities, and collaborate effectively across global teams and regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset with structured problem-solving skills, a sense of urgency, and the capacity to work independently under minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal, written, and presentation skills, paired with interpersonal abilities to influence stakeholders at all levels and advance strategic initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quick learner with adaptability to evolving technologies, regulations, and business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AML-related certifications (e.g., CAMS, CGSS) are preferred but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;$125,000 - $145,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Base salary is just one part of our total rewards package at SpaceXSI, which also includes equity, comprehensive medical, vision, and dental coverage, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, short &amp;amp; long-term disability insurance, life insurance, and various other discounts and perks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Sr. Facilities Operations Technician at SpaceXSI, you&#39;ll dive in, operating and maintaining the critical facility systems that power our supercomputing data centers. Working hands-on with MEP systems, you’ll tackle maintenance, operations, and repairs, ensuring peak performance and reliability. Expect to troubleshoot complex issues, streamline processes, and collaborate with teams to keep our infrastructure running smoothly, directly supporting xAI’s mission to accelerate human scientific discovery through AI.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently operate and maintain critical mechanical, electrical, and plumbing (MEP) systems in supercomputing data centers, ensuring high reliability and performance through hands-on maintenance, troubleshooting, and process optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform advanced maintenance and troubleshooting of critical data center systems like HVAC, power, and environmental controls, while mentoring junior technicians to ensure operational reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the maintenance and optimization of critical data center infrastructure, including power, cooling, and environmental systems, while leading a team of technicians to ensure operational reliability and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for MEP Infrastructure site safety and environmental compliance, ensuring the sites align with all local and regional health and safety requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide operational expertise for Mechanical, Electrical, and Plumbing (MEP) systems at the datacenter facility. The systems and equipment can include pumps, piping, chillers, cooling towers, CRAH units, wiring, lighting systems, generators, motors, water supply, UPS and switchgear, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Routinely inspect all areas to ensure performance measures are being maintained and proactively self-report the problems of facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with writing and executing MOPs, SOPs, EOPs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform daily inspections of critical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and maintain spare parts inventory to minimize downtime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and supervise scheduled system shutdowns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement energy monitoring metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support commissioning efforts by witnessing equipment startup, assisting with functional testing, and monitoring construction progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s Degree in Mechanical or Electrical or 6+ years of hands-on operations/facilities work experience in lieu of degree (data center experience preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of mechanical or electrical engineering principles and systems (both would be a huge plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and knowledge of all critical systems documentation including Plans, Procedures, and Operations Manuals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and knowledge of Building and Electrical Power Monitoring Systems and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PLC-based control systems and/or with Building Management Systems (Client).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication and technical writing skills in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physical Requirements:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 50 lbs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to utilize hand tools and power tools as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work is often performed in tight quarters, and physical dexterity is necessary to perform job functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 35 lbs. unassisted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working at elevated heights (up to 100 feet) with appropriate safety gear.&lt;/li&gt;
