&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;SENIOR PRODUCT MANAGER, COMMERCE PLATFORM&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Manager for our Commerce Platform, you will own product direction for the billing systems and purchase flows that power paid products across Grok, X, Grok Bot, and Cursor. This is a technical product role. You will be hands-on with the systems and able to contribute code, but your primary focus is product management for a large-scale billing system. You will do the work of a product manager, applied to building, maintaining, and triaging issues across highly scaled billing infrastructure. This high-impact role offers the opportunity to directly drive significant revenue growth while shaping systems that serve hundreds of millions of users worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product roadmap for the commerce platform billing system across Grok, X, Grok Bot, and Cursor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define requirements and drive delivery for purchase flows, including checkout, paywalls, upsell, and promotional offers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead triage of billing issues at scale. Set priorities, coordinate fixes with engineering, and close the loop with support and finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the unification of the subscription system across apps and the integration of SpaceXAI payments into the Starlink payment network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage product requirements across payment rails, including Apple App Store, Google Play, and Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute code directly where it speeds up delivery, such as prototypes, tooling, data analysis, and small fixes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track billing health and revenue metrics such as payment success rate, involuntary churn, and conversion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with legal, tax, and compliance teams on market-specific billing methods and compliance requirements to accelerate global expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience on large-scale consumer applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product management background with deep experience building large-scale, high-stakes systems (Monetization, subscriptions, or fintech, billing, payments, or transactional platforms preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical depth to read and write production code and to hold architecture discussions with engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record shipping and operating complex backend-heavy products for consumer applications at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for revenue-generating products and creating exceptional user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Apple App Store and Google Play in-app billing and Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a fast-paced, high-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience as a software engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with distributed systems, global payments infrastructure, or A/B testing frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;$180,000 - $275,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary is just one part of our total rewards package at SpaceXSI, which also includes equity, comprehensive medical, vision, and dental coverage, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, short &amp;amp; long-term disability insurance, life insurance, and various other discounts and perks.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Shipping Specialist supporting SpaceXSI data center operations, you will be responsible for the expedient, accurate movement of high-value materials and equipment (servers, GPUs, networking gear, power systems, cooling infrastructure, and other critical components) needed to support construction, commissioning, and ongoing operations. You will play a crucial role in ensuring efficient inbound and outbound logistics while maintaining product integrity, inventory accuracy, and compliance in a fast-paced, high-growth environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process inbound and outbound material through ERP/WMS systems, partnering with procurement, construction, facilities, and operations teams to ensure quality, quantity, and timely delivery of material to the floor or vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Properly package, label, and manifest parcel, LTL, and large freight shipments (including high-value/sensitive equipment) to protect product integrity throughout the transportation cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manifest consignments and schedule movements with carriers (FedEx, UPS, DHL, 3PL, expedited courier, etc.) based on delivery demand, ensuring correct documentation and configuration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with carriers and freight forwarders for pick-up and delivery; prepare shipping labels, packing slips, commercial invoices, packing lists, and other required documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify accuracy of shipping information (addresses, quantities, delivery instructions) and inspect/package products for shipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determine the most cost-effective and efficient shipping methods; track and monitor shipments to ensure on-time delivery, resolve delays/issues, and update tracking systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform cycle counts and maintain inventory accuracy in shipping-owned incoming/outgoing areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead problem-solving for transportation issues (routes, delays, customs, rush orders) and maintain system integrity for all shipments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate forklifts and material handling equipment per safety procedures to load/unload carriers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate hazardous or sensitive materials and apply appropriate packaging/transport methods based on SDS and specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with internal material handlers/drivers to expedite material and avoid cutoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong communication and customer relationships with internal requestors and destination teams; provide timely shipment updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the team to identify process improvements and recommend initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of shipping, logistics, warehousing, or materials management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in freight, expedited shipping, or high-volume manufacturing/technology/data center environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with international shipping, export regulations, and customs documentation (where applicable)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of shipping procedures, regulations, and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with shipping software (UPS WorldShip, FedEx Ship Manager, MyDHL, or similar) and ERP/WMS systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent attention to detail, organizational skills, and ability to multitask/prioritize in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and problem-solving skills; ability to work independently and collaboratively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forklift or material handling equipment certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hazmat awareness or relevant certification and knowledge of transport guidelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong computer skills (Microsoft Excel, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift 25–50 lbs. unassisted; frequent standing, walking, climbing, bending, grasping, sitting, pulling, pushing, stooping, stretching, and carrying required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be available for one of the following 12.5-hour shifts: 6:00 AM – 6:30 PM or 6:00 PM – 6:30 AM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work schedule follows a rotating pattern of 4 days on / 3 days off, then 3 days on / 4 days off (and repeating)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be open to working all required shift hours, including nights, weekends, overtime, and holidays as needed to support 24/7 operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in warehouse/data center environments with varying temperatures and noise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;br&gt;As a Site Reliability Engineer focused on campus reliability, you will design what the campus watches and trusts, technically command cross-discipline SEVs, and build the guardrails that make the next incident smaller. You are the connective tissue across compute, network, storage, power, and cooling on one of the largest AI training campuses in the world. This role demands calm incident leadership, fleet-scale observability judgment, and the ability to drive reliability work across software and facility boundaries. We are looking for candidates from power plants, nuclear power plants, data centers, or people who currently work or have worked in facilities like SpaceXSI with power, compute, cooling, and related plant systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own monitoring architecture and signal quality across GPU and host telemetry (DCGM, Prometheus/Grafana) and facility telemetry (BMS, EPMS, DCIM, SCADA, CDU / direct liquid cooling): what we alert on, suppress, and trust. Consume NOC noise-disposition feedback to drive suppression and redesign. Treat alert noise as a design failure, not an operator failure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide SEV command support: technical incident leadership, bridge coordination with the NOC, paging and escalation (e.g., PagerDuty), and timeline and severity hygiene.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run blameless postmortems and drive corrective actions to closed, not filed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gate high-risk change: fleet-scale firmware/BIOS/BMC rollouts (Redfish, canaries, rollback) and SOP/MOP/EOP-governed work on power and cooling systems through a disciplined change management process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional reliability projects spanning compute, network (InfiniBand/RoCE), storage, and facility signal boundaries, including grey failures that cross those boundaries (e.g., NVLink flapping, thermal throttling, power sequencing).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Hardware Failure Analysis on systemic failure classes: turn fleet data (MTBF/AFR, repeat-RMA trends) into monitoring, stop-rules, and vendor RCA inputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain playbooks, run game days, and keep cross-discipline dependency maps current. Own runbook quality jointly with the NOC (SRE designs; NOC operates and corrects).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define error budgets and availability objectives at campus and service boundaries as adopted by the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in on-call rotations and incident response for SEV-class events in the Memphis / Southaven data center campus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PROFILE SIGNALS:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in power plants, nuclear power plants, data centers, or facilities like SpaceXSI — current or prior — spanning power, compute, cooling, or related plant systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven large-scale incident command experience and calm technical leadership on a bridge. Nuclear control-room, shift supervisor / Senior Reactor Operator (SRO), Shift Technical Advisor, or Navy nuclear experience counts as incident command.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated monitoring and observability design at fleet or campus scale, including alert hygiene, suppression, and signal quality. Treats alert noise as a design failure, not an operator failure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-team facilitation and systems engineering depth across software and facility boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SUCCESS MEASURED BY:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MTTD / MTTR trend for SEV-class events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;% of SEVs with a blameless postmortem and closed action items&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alert actionable ratio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recurrence rate of incident classes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring coverage of critical dependencies across compute, network, storage, power, and cooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GPU fleet availability lost to infrastructure events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Systems Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or a related field (or equivalent experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in site reliability, systems engineering, plant operations, or large-scale production operations, preferably in power plants, nuclear power plants, high-performance computing, or data center environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven large-scale incident command experience and calm technical leadership on a bridge, whether from an SRE/NOC bridge or a plant control room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated monitoring and observability design at fleet or campus scale, including alert hygiene, suppression, and signal quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with at least one of: Prometheus/Grafana, NVIDIA DCGM, or industrial telemetry and controls (SCADA, BMS/BAS, EPMS, DCIM, PLCs, Modbus/BACnet).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across at least two of: compute, network, storage, power, and cooling / facilities telemetry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing and operating playbooks, runbooks, or SOP/MOP/EOPs with a 24/7 operations, control room, or NOC partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in scripting (Python, Bash) for automation and analysis, plus general experience in at least one systems language (C, C++, Java, Go, Rust, or similar). Not required to be expert in all of them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving skills with a data-driven approach to reliability engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively with cross-functional teams, including NOC, data center operations, hardware failure analysis, and infrastructure engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in power plants, nuclear power plants, or other high-consequence industrial control environments (ICS/OT).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current or prior work in data centers or facilities like SpaceXSI spanning power, compute, cooling, and related plant systems, including CDU / direct liquid cooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in AI/ML infrastructure or supercomputing environments: GB200/NVL72 or H100/H200-class GPU fleets, NCCL, InfiniBand/RoCE, Slurm or Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fleet firmware and BMC management (Redfish, IPMI), including firmware release validation and staged rollouts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliability engineering methods: MTBF/AFR analysis, reliability-centered maintenance, grey-failure diagnosis, and vendor RCA/RMA partnership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CMMS (e.g., Maximo) and commissioning / integrated systems testing (IST) and operational turnover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on definition and use of SLOs, SLIs, and error budgets at service or campus boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running game days, dependency mapping, and closed-loop corrective action programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data center hardware and plant signals (servers, GPUs, networking, power, cooling) in addition to software telemetry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work in a fast-paced startup or tech company like SpaceXSI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;X Ads is one of the highest-leverage product areas at X. You’ll work on systems that operate at massive scale, directly affect the business, and are being rebuilt with modern infrastructure and AI at the center.&amp;nbsp;This is an opportunity to join a small, fast-moving team where early-career engineers can take on real ownership, learn from strong engineers, and ship products that matter.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We’re looking for high-slope software engineers who want to help rebuild and transform the X Ads Platform using SpaceXSI&#39;s infrastructure and AI stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is a great fit for engineers who are early in their careers but learn quickly, ship fast, and want to work on products and systems that operate at massive scale. You do not need to have deep ads experience already, but you should be excited to learn how large-scale advertising systems work and how AI can make ads more relevant, useful, and effective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work across product, backend systems, infrastructure, and AI-powered features that directly impact the majority of X’s revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
