&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Software Engineering Intern/Freshman/Sophomore: $30 USD per hour   &amp;nbsp; &lt;br&gt;Software Engineering Intern/Junior/Senior: $34 USD per hour&lt;br&gt;Software Engineering Intern/Completed Bachelor&#39;s: $36 USD per hour&lt;br&gt;Software Engineering Intern/Completed Master&#39;s: $38 USD per hour &amp;nbsp; &lt;br&gt;Software Engineering Intern/Completed PhD: $40 USD per hour&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your salary will be determined by academic level. Hourly pay is just one part of our total rewards package at SpaceXSI. You may also be eligible for a stipend to subsidize relocation costs, as well as access to our comprehensive medical coverage and a 401(k) retirement plan.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SUPERVISOR, FACILITIES OPERATIONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Facilities Operations Supervisor at SpaceXSI Memphis, you will oversee the maintenance and performance of critical data center infrastructure, including power, cooling, and environmental systems. You will lead a team of Facilities Operations Technicians, driving hands-on technical operations, team leadership, process optimization, and cross-functional collaboration to ensure the reliability and efficiency of our data center. This role emphasizes fostering a team-first culture, prioritizing team focus, and promoting a collaborative work environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and mentor a team of Facilities Operations Technicians, fostering a culture of excellence, collaboration, and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee maintenance, monitoring, and troubleshooting of data center infrastructure, including HVAC, power distribution, and backup systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement, and optimize preventive maintenance schedules, equipment calibration, and system performance monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and enforce standard operating procedures (SOPs) to ensure operational consistency and efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with safety regulations and industry standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering and procurement teams to streamline equipment intake, installation, and maintenance processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize internal applications for inventory and asset management, ensuring accurate tracking and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage critical equipment maintenance and repairs, ensuring timely resolution and detailed documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams to support seamless data center operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead initiatives to enhance operational efficiency and minimize downtime&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide on-call support and respond promptly to critical facilities incidents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in mechanical, electrical, or engineering field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience managing critical facilities systems, including power, cooling, and environmental controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience troubleshooting and maintaining critical facilities infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience programming PLC-based control systems or working with building management systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project Management Professional (PMP) certification or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EPA Universal Refrigerant Certification (EPA 608 Technician)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of electrical, mechanical, and HVAC systems in data centers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with building management systems (BMS) and environmental monitoring tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven leadership experience in critical facilities or technical operations environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead facilities infrastructure projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with hand tools and power tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong prioritization and time management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment while maintaining attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must pass pre-employment and annual post-employment background checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 35 lbs. unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in environments with exposure to noise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working at heights up to 50 feet with appropriate safety gear&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physical dexterity to perform job functions in confined spaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Availability to work evenings and weekends based on site operational needs; flexibility is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver’s license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceXSI is building and operating one of the world’s largest AI training campuses in Memphis, including Colossus and site facilities that support it. As a Facilities Supervisor, you will lead a team of technicians and specialist for an assigned area of that campus—office and support buildings, site infrastructure, and grounds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your leadership keeps work orders moving, preventive maintenance on schedule, and building systems (HVAC, plumbing, electrical, general repair) in working order. Depending on assignment, you may also own soft services such as trash, landscaping, and pest control. This is hands-on front-line leadership for facilities maintenance. Your time will be spent between being on the floor with technicians, vendors, and tickets—closing work, removing blockers, and holding an exceptional standard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a high-performing team handling facilities maintenance for an assigned campus area—including general maintenance, HVAC, plumbing, electrical, and (where assigned) janitorial, landscaping, waste, and pest control—to deliver reliable service with minimal disruption to occupied buildings and site operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own day-to-day work orders and preventive maintenance: prioritize tickets, staff the work, inspect quality, and drive closeout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage third-party vendors (e.g., janitorial, landscaping, pest control, repair contractors) to enforce corporate standards, optimize contracts, and maintain service levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee maintenance, repairs, and installations across assigned buildings and grounds—offices, support facilities, and site infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute a proactive preventive maintenance program for assigned assets, minimizing downtime and maximizing efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor small construction and site-improvement work to ensure on-time, on-budget delivery with zero impact to ongoing operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach, develop, and hold a team of maintenance technicians to safety, quality, and productivity standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize tasks dynamically in a fast-paced environment, eliminate blockers, and drive continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional experience with facilities maintenance or facilities management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience leading a team or project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in construction management, engineering, facilities management, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven vendor management skills, with a track record of holding contractors to scope, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise with work-order / asset management software and building systems (HVAC, plumbing, electrical, fire suppression).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail, relentless focus on cleanliness and standards, and ability to thrive independently in dynamic, deadline-driven settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on background as a technician or tradesperson (HVAC, plumbing, electrical, or general maintenance) before moving into leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovative problem-solver who anticipates needs and drives efficiency in high-volume, 24/7 environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based at the Memphis, TN campus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to provide 24/7 on-call support for emergencies and critical facility issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and willingness to work extended hours, weekends, and non-standard schedules as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in temperatures over 80 degrees as required by the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

