&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will involve the supervision of a team of hourly employees operating within SpaceXSI&#39;s logistics organization. Our goal is to become a leader in logistics performance with high inventory efficiency/accuracy and industry leading customer service while maintaining a safe work environment that utilizes the latest in applicable technologies. This supervisor will also be responsible for leading and driving continuous improvement throughout all aspects of their operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage an hourly workforce by assessing employee performance, providing positive/constructive feedback, facilitating conflict resolution, and addressing repeat issues with corrective actions, performance improvement plans or through disciplinary means&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead by setting an example, taking feedback from all levels of the organization, and motivating your organization to achieve the highest level of results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and improve operations, ensuring a safe work environment with the goal of zero OSHA recordable annually&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the incoming acceptance, storing, and issuing of a wide variety of parts, details, and hardware into inventory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage operations that provide industry leading levels of customer service in all operations: recognizing the needs of the business and adapting to support our mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cost saving opportunities, identifying internal/external cost reductions and optimization opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure cycle counting procedures are routinely followed to meet both our internal and external audit requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain the appropriate service routes and material replenishments to deliver material to internal customers at agreed upon service levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise the local shipping and receiving operation; coordinate movements into and out of the local facility, along with critical point to point movements outside of the local facility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive projects and changes that contribute to logistics ongoing improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure procedures are routinely being followed for shelf-life storage and maintaining proper rotation of stock and FIFO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the appropriate environmental controls are continuously effective, depending on the material requirements of the items being stored&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively monitor and grow the workforce, ensuring team members are challenged and performing at the expected standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and approve employee time keeping records&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree and 2+ years of professional experience in materials management, supply chain, or production/manufacturing; or 4+ years of professional experience in materials management, supply chain, or production/manufacturing in lieu of a degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience working with enterprise resource planning (ERP)/inventory management software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with material requirements planning (MRP) systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of leadership experience within materials management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using WarpDrive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completion of a leadership or rotational development program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Association for supply chain management (APICS) certification – certified in production and inventory management (CPIM) or certified supply chain professional (CSCP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lean/6-Sigma experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Green/black belt certifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate forklift equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and team-building skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and self-driven, capable of working independently with little direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced/cross-functional environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within an aerospace, aviation, or automotive manufacturing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with Microsoft Office applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a high-stress environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good response to challenges posed by short deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acute attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifting up to 25 lbs. (unassisted), standing, climbing, bending, grasping, sitting, pulling, pushing stooping, stretching and carrying are generally required to perform the functions of this position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to travel to other sites, as required (up to 25%)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be available for one of the following 12.5-hour shifts: 6:00 AM – 6:30 PM or 6:00 PM – 6:30 AM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work schedule follows a rotating pattern of 4 days on / 3 days off, then 3 days on / 4 days off (and repeating)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Supervisor, OSP Fiber will lead a team of five fiber technicians responsible for installing, splicing, testing, and maintaining outside plant fiber infrastructure for a new data center. This is a hands-on leadership role: you will set daily priorities, own crew safety and quality, and still work in the field alongside the team. You will be accountable for schedule, as-built accuracy, and delivering a reliable OSP fiber plant from construction through turnover and ongoing operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, train, schedule, and develop a team of fiber technicians; provide coaching, performance feedback, and coverage planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and assign daily OSP work (aerial and underground placement, vault/handhole work, splicing, terminations, and testing) to meet data center construction and cutover schedules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead by example as a working supervisor; perform splicing, testing, and field work as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce safety, PPE, lockout, traffic control, and utility-locate practices; stop work when conditions are unsafe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own quality of splices, OTDR/OLTS results, labeling, and as-built records; drive rework to zero&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with OSP engineering, construction, utilities, and data center teams on design changes, access, and outage windows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track production, quality, and material usage; report status, risks, and resource needs to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage tools, fusion splicers, test equipment, vehicles, and fiber/consumable inventory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure field work matches issued drawings and company standards; capture redlines and close as-builts with engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support commissioning, emergency restoration, and after-hours work as required for a 24/7 data center environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in fiber optic OSP installation, splicing, testing, or maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience leading technicians (supervisor, foreman, or team lead)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on proficiency with fusion splicing and fiber test equipment (OTDR, OLTS, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing and able to work in the field, including outdoor construction conditions, and to work nights, weekends, or overtime as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate’s degree or trade certification in fiber optics, telecommunications, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supervising OSP or data center fiber crews through new site build-out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fiber certifications (FOA CFOT, BICSI, Corning, AFL, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with aerial and buried fiber, conduit/duct banks, vaults, handholes, and building-entrance laterals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with TIA/BICSI guidelines, NESC, locates, and local permitting/construction practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read OSP drawings, splice diagrams, and GIS/route maps and to produce accurate field redlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;OSHA 10/30, first aid/CPR, or similar safety training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, timekeeping, and work-order discipline; comfortable coordinating vendors and construction trades&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience standing up a new team, including hiring, training plans, and tool/equipment setup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule varies depending on site operational needs; frequent overtime and weekend support is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to perform job duties that require standing, kneeling, crouching, twisting upper body, working in cramped positions, climbing, lifting up to 50 lbs., and working on ladders/lifts at elevated heights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in an environment requiring exposure to fumes, odors, noise, heat, cold, and rain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to rapidly change roles/responsibilities while working in a high-paced, challenging work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SUPERVISOR, PORTER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Supervisor, Porter is a personnel management role responsible for the processes of ordering, receiving product, equipment, event support, managing inventory, tracking spends, and ensuring product and supplies are readily available in the necessary areas for the food services department. This role is also responsible for the scheduling and payroll management, as well as assignment of responsibilities and overall staff supervision of the porter team. The Porter Supervisor supports the mission by coordinating the logistics of the perishable and non-perishable resources utilized by our Culinary and Food &amp;amp; Beverage team. They also that all food safety and quality assurance best practices are being followed. Additionally, they perform all of the heavy lifting for event setup, product, and equipment transport, to support with the necessary day to day operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct on-hand inventories and place orders for all concept areas of culinary food services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive and inspect deliveries from vendors daily&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and enforce standards for ordering and receiving operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate inventory records for all departmental areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create awareness among kitchen teams regarding inaccuracies in product deliveries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the culinary team to ensure optimal product and vendor selection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and track departmental spending by vendor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile invoices and submit purchase orders for food and equipment vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fulfill interdepartmental requests through the internal request system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage porters to provide site support, handle food deliveries, and maintain cleanliness of surrounding areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support events and operations by moving equipment, setting up, and resetting event spaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Move equipment to and from the warehouse to meet site needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain cleanliness of operational areas and report maintenance issues for repair&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage dishwashers to support kitchen operations and maintain cleanliness of the kitchen and surrounding areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage staff scheduling, payroll, and attendance for the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct annual staff performance reviews and provide ongoing coaching and development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all staff training and credentials remain up to date&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise deliveries of water, ice, and backstock supplies across campus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal delivery of supplies for daily operations and events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a safe and clean work environment for the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor equipment and asset management, including preventative maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support daily services and perform other tasks as directed by management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of inventory experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of restaurant or retail food service experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of leadership experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have or be able to obtain TX food handler card&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have or be able to obtain manager level food safety certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a corporate environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in large team settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer service and or guest interaction experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data entry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with inventory management software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong writing and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail oriented and organized&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to carry large heavy items unassisted (up to 25 lbs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to stand for long periods of time (up to 10 hours a day)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work all shifts and available for overtime, weekends and holiday(s) as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to travel to other SpaceX locations for significant/extended periods of time as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to perform frequent bending, stooping, and lifting of objects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to participate in internal leadership and development training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand: Up to 10 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sit: Up to 3 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Push/Pull: Up to 50 lbs (unassisted) 2 hours or longer per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overhead reach: Up to 1 hour per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Walk: Up to 3 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lift/Carry: Up to 25 lbs (unassisted) 2 hours or longer per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Climb (ladder/stairs): Up to 1 hour per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kneel/Crouch: Up to 6 hours per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Upper body twist: Up to 1 hour per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in temperatures over 80 degrees up to 1 hour per day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidate must be capable of safely performing the physical requirements of the job listed in the job description.&amp;nbsp;Candidate may be required to complete a pre-employment questionnaire and/or physical to confirm these capabilities, which may include a medical history review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Starting base salary is $100,000 USD&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your actual level and base salary will be determined on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on the following considerations: job-related knowledge and skills, education, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary is just one part of our total rewards package at SpaceXSI which includes comprehensive medical, vision, and dental coverage, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, short &amp;amp; long-term disability insurance, life insurance, and various other discounts and perks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR &lt;a class=&quot;notion-link-token notion-focusable-token notion-enable-hover&quot; href=&quot;https://deccs.pmddtc.state.gov/deccs&quot; data-token-index=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;link-annotation-unknown-block-id--1213793699&quot;&gt;here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Supervisor on the power generation team, you will lead the technicians who operate, maintain, and repair on-site generation that powers SpaceXSI&#39;s high-density AI supercomputing facilities. You will oversee plant technicians, process technicians, and electrical technicians as one operations and maintenance team — covering gas turbine packages, balance-of-plant, process/fluid systems, and plant electrical systems through 34.5 kV.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will operate with autonomy to solve diverse and complex problems, manage multiple workstreams at once, and work in a dynamic, fast-paced plant environment. This role directly impacts reliability, safety, and uptime at the Southaven and Memphis sites. You will keep generation online, keep maintenance disciplined and cost-effective, and build a technician team that can respond to trips, outages, and commissioning without losing the day-to-day plant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a team of plant technicians, process technicians, and electrical technicians responsible for inspections, testing, operations, maintenance, and repair of power generation systems, including gas turbines and generators, balance-of-plant, fuel gas and process/fluid systems, water and compressed/instrument air, HVAC and cooling, and plant electrical systems up to 13.5 kV / 34.5 kV&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule daily work, prioritize assignments, and balance planned maintenance against real-time plant needs, alarms, trips, and outages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct switching, isolation, LOTO, start-up, shutdown, and restoration activities so electrical, mechanical, and process work is coordinated and safe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own work execution quality: procedures, work orders, as-found/as-left records, and close-out in the CMMS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Know and enforce SpaceXSI safety procedures, including LOTO, NFPA 70E / arc-flash, confined space, and hot work; stop work when conditions are unsafe and escalate uncorrected hazards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support plant start-ups, shutdowns, commissioning, and outages alongside engineering, operations, and contractors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with engineering, operators, and utility personnel on clearances, switching, and work that affects generation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee vendors and contractors supporting the plant; keep work competitive, safe, and on schedule, and coordinate with buyers and accounts payable as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate with the Manager on daily activities, plant status, team performance, and issues requiring escalation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive overall technician performance and effectiveness through coaching, development, and clear standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of hands on experience working in a power plant, generating station, or other high-reliability industrial facility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate’s or bachelor’s degree in a technical, construction, or engineering field, or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on background in one or more of: gas turbine / plant operations, process or fluid systems (fuel gas, water, compressed air), or medium-voltage electrical operations and maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a mixed-discipline operations and maintenance team (mechanical, process, and electrical)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read P&amp;amp;IDs, single-line diagrams, electrical schematics, and equipment O&amp;amp;M manual&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with LOTO, switching procedures, and NFPA 70E / arc-flash practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using a CMMS or work-order system to plan, schedule, and close maintenance work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft applications such as Excel, Outlook, Word, and PowerPoint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing budgets, third-party vendors, and contractor work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail, documentation, and plant housekeeping standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently with little direction and to meet deadlines in a fast-paced, ever-changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to anticipate plant needs and develop practical solutions for reliability and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to perform hands-on work in all environments (heat, cold, rain), in tight quarters or at heights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work extended hours, nights, weekends, and on-call schedules to support plant operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remain focused while working in hazardous environments, while wearing appropriate PPE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to lift up to 25 lbs unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifting, standing, climbing, bending, grasping, sitting, pulling, pushing, stooping, stretching, and carrying are generally required to perform the functions of this position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work on-site at the power generation facility, with potential travel to other SpaceXSI sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver’s license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role supervises hourly Production Coordinators and adjacent logistics teammates supporting data center construction, commissioning, and ongoing campus operations at Memphis / Southaven. You will lead shift execution of work-order driven material flow — inventory requests, shortage management, kit / de-kit, BOM reconciliation, and on-time delivery of high-value servers, networking gear, power and cooling components, and infrastructure materials to Site Operations and construction. You will set the standard for inventory integrity, safety, and customer service while driving continuous improvement across receiving, inventory, kitting, and material flow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage an hourly workforce by assessing employee performance, providing positive and constructive feedback, facilitating conflict resolution, and addressing repeat issues through corrective actions, performance improvement plans, or disciplinary means&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead by setting an example, taking feedback from all levels of the organization, and motivating the team to achieve the highest level of results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and improve operations, ensuring a safe work environment with the goal of zero OSHA recordables annually&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own shift-level production coordination: inventory requests from work orders, kits, and replacement parts; planning and shortage management; and on-time material delivery for data center build and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure parts and equipment are handled and protected to SpaceXAI specifications, including high-value servers, networking gear, power and cooling components, and infrastructure materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with engineers, technicians, Site Operations, and construction on work-order and material-request priorities; communicate part status and estimated completion dates to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure work-order bill of material quantities are reconciled and that material released to production matches paperwork (damage, part numbers, quantity, revisions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain high integrity in company computer systems; drive resolution of incorrect system data that creates bad demand, schedules, or operational failure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise kit build, de-kit, return-to-stock, staging, and workflow improvements across receiving, inventory, and material flow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure cycle counting, FIFO / stock rotation, and environmental controls are followed for materials under the team’s care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cost-saving and continuous-improvement projects across production coordination and logistics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively develop the workforce and monitor and approve employee timekeeping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree and 2+ years of professional experience in materials management, supply chain, or production/manufacturing; or 4+ years of professional experience in materials management, supply chain, or production/manufacturing in lieu of a degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience leading or supervising hourly warehouse, inventory, production coordination, or manufacturing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience working with ERP / inventory management software (SAP, Oracle, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with MRP systems and work-order / BOM-driven material flow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of leadership experience within materials management or production coordination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in data center, aerospace, automotive, semiconductor, or electronic manufacturing environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;APICS certification (CPIM or CSCP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lean / Six Sigma experience; Green or Black Belt preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate forklift equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and team-building skills; organized, self-driven, and effective in a fast-paced cross-functional environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing and able to work one or more of the following shifts; preference for candidates flexible across all four shifts, including nights, weekends, and overtime as site needs require:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shift A:&lt;/strong&gt; 6:00 AM – 6:30 PM, Sunday–Wednesday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shift B:&lt;/strong&gt; 6:00 AM – 6:30 PM, Wednesday–Saturday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shift C:&lt;/strong&gt; 6:00 PM – 6:30 AM, Sunday–Wednesday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shift D:&lt;/strong&gt; 6:00 PM – 6:30 AM, Wednesday–Saturday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver’s license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work at elevated heights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in extreme outdoor environments — heat, cold, rain, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in an environment requiring exposure to fumes, odors, and noise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to operate machinery such as forklifts and loaders when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to and available for travel (up to 20% of time)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work onsite in the Memphis, TN / Southaven, MS area&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SUPERVISOR, SAFETY OPERATIONS (CHILD SAFETY)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SpaceXSI’s Safety team protects free expression while ensuring our users can safely and successfully engage with our platform through robust policy enforcement. Child Safety is our highest-stakes area: the team identifies, investigates, and removes child safety related abuse across X, Grok and X Money products, including AI-generated content, and makes the legally required reports to NCMEC. As we increasingly leverage AI-based automation, we innovate and experiment at a fast pace, striving to be a learning organization with a growth mindset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Supervisor, Child Safety, you will lead the Austin-based Child Safety analyst team across shifts. You will be hands-on with escalations, improve the team quality and defensibility of every high-risk decision, and coordinate with Safety leadership, Legal, and law enforcement response teams on high-profile cases. You will lead the team’s shift from scaled manual review to analysts focused on “Automation First” appeals, model evaluations and audits, investigations, and escalations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the Austin-based Child Safety team, a team of analysts (including senior analysts) covering X, Grok and X Money, with consistent standards across all shifts and strict adherence to SLAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the escalation layer for Child Safety: be hands-on with complex, urgent, and high-profile cases, including high profile accounts, internal escalations from law enforcement response and legal teams, and SpacexSI products incident escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own NCMEC reporting decisions for the team. Ensure every enforcement decision is accurate, well-documented, and meets legal obligations, Bring thoughtful, well-reasoned recommendations to leadership on escalations, balancing the protection of minors with SpaceXSI’s free speech principles&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the team’s response to viral incidents and emerging abuse trends: track results, and escalate patterns quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take an automation-first approach. Partner with Program Leads to calibrate classifiers and turn findings into concrete improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the team’s automation evaluations, audits, and labeling ensuring high-quality curated data&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use querying languages (e.g., SQL or Python) and LLM-powered agents to analyze operational data, identify trends, and drive data-informed improvements to policies and processes. Build that habit across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own your dashboards and KPIs: know hour to hour how the backlog and escalation queues are doing, and keep a baseline to spot and investigate anomalies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep shift handovers, operational process documentation, and team performance trackers&amp;nbsp; current so every analyst works from the same playbook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide coaching, mentorship, and professional development to foster critical thinking, efficiency, growth, retention, and wellbeing in a team regularly exposed to highly sensitive content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run strong feedback loops as a proactive manager: give constructive feedback early and often, out of a desire to improve, and take it in stride&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the team into child safety subject matter experts with a defensibility mindset, so every decision can be explained and defended&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own team performance end to end: set clear expectations, measure them, reward strong performers, and act quickly and fairly on underperformance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal stakeholders (e.g., HR, workforce management, Legal, Policy, other Safety teams) to align on Child Safety objectives and coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All other duties and responsibilities as required by business need&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASIC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in online child safety, Trust &amp;amp; Safety operations, criminal investigations, or another safety field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience leading or supervising a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise in identifying and investigating CSAM, CSE and non-CSE related child safety areas, including grooming behaviors and risks in AI-generated content, with strong knowledge of legal obligations (such as NCMEC reporting) and industry standards for protecting minors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in crisis and escalation management, with the ability to make sound, defensible decisions under pressure and navigate ambiguity in time-sensitive, high-impact situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to apply SpaceXSI safety policies with judgment, weighing the protection of minors against free expression in the global public square&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in data analysis with hands-on experience using LLMs, SQL, or Python to extract insights, identify emerging abuse vectors, and optimize operational performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about AI and automation, with an interest in leveraging technology to improve Child Safety enforcement and reduce manual workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong communicator who can articulate business needs, write clear escalation summaries, and build relationships with Legal, Policy, Engineering, and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An active X - including Grok - user with a deep understanding of the platform’s role as a global public square and its Safety challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A lifelong learner who reflects on their gaps, strives to fill them, and is curious about how to improve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A team player who places the interests of the team first and balances mission accomplishment with compassion for their people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing Child Safety or Trust &amp;amp; Safety teams at a social media or generative AI company, leveraging AI or other automation tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in leading red-teaming and adversarial testing of Large Language Models to proactively identify novel abuse vectors, jailbreaks, and safety failure modes, with a proven ability to translate findings into concrete improvements for enforcement systems, team processes, and platform robustness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience providing human oversight and insights for scaled agentic AI operations, with abilities in prompting and evaluating LLM agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will be on-site at our Austin, TX office, and might require off-shift support, including weekends as business needs arise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role may involve exposure to sensitive or graphic content, including vulgar language, violent threats, pornography, and other graphic images&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be willing to travel occasionally to collaborate with global teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

